(window.UPANISHAD_DATA=window.UPANISHAD_DATA||{})["sandilya"]={"slug":"sandilya","name":"Śāṇḍilya","deva":"शाण्डिल्य","note":"selected verses","intro":["The Complete Text<br>Three Adhyāyas · 66 Verses · Comprehensive Prose Sections<br>Word-by-Word Word-by-Word for Key Verses · Visual Analysis<br><br>Atharva Veda · 58th in the Muktikā 108<br>The Most Comprehensive of the Yoga Upaniṣads","The Śāṇḍilya Upaniṣad (शाण्डिल्योपनिषत्) is one of the longest and most comprehensive Yoga Upaniṣads. It is attached to the Atharva Veda and is the 58th of the 108 Upaniṣads in the Muktikā's canonical list. Among the 20 Yoga Upaniṣads, it is widely regarded as the most systematic treatment of the eight-limbed yoga (aṣṭāṅga-yoga) outside of Patañjali himself."],"sections":[{"t":"Introduction","u":[{"ref":"1. About the Śāṇḍilya Upaniṣad","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The Śāṇḍilya Upaniṣad (शाण्डिल्योपनिषत्) is one of the longest and most comprehensive Yoga Upaniṣads. It is attached to the Atharva Veda and is the 58th of the 108 Upaniṣads in the Muktikā's canonical list. Among the 20 Yoga Upaniṣads, it is widely regarded as the most systematic treatment of the eight-limbed yoga (aṣṭāṅga-yoga) outside of Patañjali himself.","The text takes the form of a dialogue between the sage Śāṇḍilya and the seer Atharvan. Śāṇḍilya is one of the great ancestral ṛṣis (named in the famous Śāṇḍilya-Vidyā of the Chāndogya Upaniṣad 3.14) and the lineage-ancestor of an entire family of brāhmaṇas. Atharvan, the first sage of the Atharva Veda, is here cast as the teacher.","Three adhyāyas (chapters) structure the text:","Adhyāya 1 — by far the longest — gives a comprehensive treatment of the eight limbs of yoga, with detailed sub-treatments of: 10 yamas, 10 niyamas, 8 āsanas, the subtle anatomy of 14 nāḍīs and 10 vāyus, prāṇāyāma, pratyāhāra (with 18 marma-points), dhāraṇā, dhyāna, and samādhi.","Adhyāya 2 — short — Atharvan teaches Śāṇḍilya the brahma-vidyā: the knowledge of Brahman as Truth-Knowledge-Bliss, ungraspable, indescribable, \"tat tvam asi.\"","Adhyāya 3 — medium — Atharvan describes the three forms of Brahman (niṣkala, sakala-niṣkala, sakala) and concludes with four verses on Dattātreya."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"2. Place in the Yoga Upaniṣad Canon","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Among the 20 Yoga Upaniṣads, Śāṇḍilya occupies a unique position:","Most systematic treatment of the eight limbs — closer to Patañjali than any other Yoga Upaniṣad","Expansion of the yamas and niyamas to 10 each (Patañjali has 5 each)","Detailed subtle-body anatomy: 14 nāḍīs and 10 vāyus, with their precise locations and functions","Long verse-section (§7 in Adhyāya 1) with 51 verses on prāṇāyāma stages, the Khecarī and Vaiṣṇavī Mudrās, manonmanī state, and the mind's dissolution","Synthesis with brahma-vidyā — most Yoga Upaniṣads stay practical; Śāṇḍilya integrates the practice with explicit Vedānta teaching","Sri Aurobindo references the Śāṇḍilya Upaniṣad as a key source for the systematic understanding of yogic anatomy. Modern teachers (Sivananda, Vishnudevananda, Krishnamacharya's lineage) draw on its material."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"3. Structural Overview","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Structure of the Śāṇḍilya Upaniṣad across its three Adhyāyas"],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"4. The Ten Yamas (Adhyāya 1, §1)","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The ten ethical restraints","The Śāṇḍilya Upaniṣad expands the classical five yamas of Patañjali into ten. The ordering and definitions are unique to this text:","<table><tr><td>#</td><td>Yama</td><td>Sanskrit</td><td>Definition (per text)</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Ahiṃsā</td><td>अहिंसा</td><td>Not causing pain to any being, at any time, through mind/speech/body</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Satya</td><td>सत्य</td><td>Speech that conforms to reality AND is beneficial</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Asteya</td><td>अस्तेय</td><td>Freedom from desire for others' property</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Brahmacarya</td><td>ब्रह्मचर्य</td><td>Abstention from sexual contact in all conditions</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Dayā</td><td>दया</td><td>Compassion toward all beings</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Ārjava</td><td>आर्जव</td><td>Uniformity of action in mind, speech, body</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Kṣamā</td><td>क्षमा</td><td>Patient bearing of all things — pleasant and unpleasant</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Dhṛti</td><td>धृति</td><td>Mental steadiness in loss, separation, attainment</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Mitāhāra</td><td>मिताहार</td><td>Soft, sweet food; leave one-fourth of stomach empty</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Śauca</td><td>शौच</td><td>External (earth/water) and Internal (Self-knowledge)</td></tr></table>","Notable feature: Satya is defined as \"what is real AND beneficial\" — not \"the literal truth at all costs.\" If a truth would harm a being, it is not satya. This is the Vedic ethical formulation, distinct from absolutist truth-telling."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"5. The Ten Niyamas (Adhyāya 1, §2)","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The ten personal observances","Likewise, the niyamas are expanded to ten:","<table><tr><td>#</td><td>Niyama</td><td>Sanskrit</td><td>Definition (per text)</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>Tapas</td><td>तपस्</td><td>Body-emaciation through kṛcchra, cāndrāyaṇa</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Santoṣa</td><td>सन्तोष</td><td>Satisfaction with whatever comes by itself</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Āstikya</td><td>आस्तिक्य</td><td>Faith in Vedic dharma</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Dāna</td><td>दान</td><td>Giving rightly-earned wealth with faith</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Īśvara-pūjana</td><td>ईश्वरपूजन</td><td>Worship of Viṣṇu, Rudra, etc.</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Siddhānta-śravaṇa</td><td>सिद्धान्तश्रवण</td><td>Inquiry into Vedānta</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Hrī</td><td>ह्री</td><td>Shame at acts contrary to Veda/world</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Mati</td><td>मति</td><td>Firm conviction in Vedic course</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Japa</td><td>जप</td><td>Mantra-repetition (loud, whisper, mental)</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Vrata</td><td>व्रत</td><td>Regularity in prescribed actions</td></tr></table>","Especially notable: japa is given three levels of efficacy: verbal-loud (1×), whispered (1,000×), mental (10,000,000×). This is the foundational scriptural source for the universal yogic teaching that the more interior the practice, the greater its potency."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"6. The Eight Āsanas (Adhyāya 1, §3)","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The eight āsanas with their distinct purposes","The Śāṇḍilya enumerates eight āsanas. Notably, Mayūrāsana (\"peacock pose\") is included — one of the earliest Yoga Upaniṣad references to a non-seated āsana."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"7. The Fourteen Nāḍīs (Adhyāya 1, §4)","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The fourteen principal nāḍīs","The Śāṇḍilya provides one of the most detailed accounts of the subtle-body channels (nāḍīs) in the entire Upaniṣadic corpus. Fourteen principal nāḍīs are identified, with three primary (Iḍā, Piṅgalā, Suṣumnā). The text says:","\"Suṣumnā is the universal supporter (viśva-dhāriṇī) and is called the path of liberation. Behind the anus, supported on the spinal column, extending to the head — it is to be known in the brahmarandhra as manifest, subtle, the Vaiṣṇavī.\"","Iḍā carries the moon (tamas, the portion of nectar); Piṅgalā carries the sun (rajas, the portion of poison); Suṣumnā devours time itself. Liberation comes when prāṇa enters Suṣumnā."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"8. The Ten Vāyus (Adhyāya 1, §4)","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The five principal and five subsidiary vāyus","Five primary vāyus (Prāṇa, Apāna, Samāna, Udāna, Vyāna) and five subsidiary vāyus (Nāga, Kūrma, Kṛkara, Devadatta, Dhanañjaya) together govern all physiological functions in the subtle body."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"9. The Eighteen Marma-Sthānas (Adhyāya 1, §8)","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Sites of pratyāhāra — ascending and descending","In the pratyāhāra section, the Śāṇḍilya enumerates eighteen vital points (marma-sthānas) at which the yogi sequentially holds awareness — moving up the body and down. This is the most concrete pratyāhāra-method given in any Yoga Upaniṣad."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"10. The Three Forms of Brahman (Adhyāya 3)","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Niṣkala, Sakala-Niṣkala, Sakala — the three modes of Brahman","Adhyāya 3 distinguishes three forms of Brahman:","Niṣkala (without parts) — the supreme transcendent: Truth, Knowledge, Bliss; motionless, stainless, all-pervading","Sakala-Niṣkala (mixed) — the Lord (Īśvara) accompanied by his innate avidyā / māyā (the three-colored prakṛti)","Sakala (with parts) — the manifest divine form: here, the four-armed Dattātreya, blue-lotus-like, fierce against sin","This three-fold scheme integrates the apophatic Brahman of Vedānta with the iconic Dattātreya — a synthesis characteristic of late Upaniṣadic literature."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Key Verses with Word-by-Word","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Twelve foundational verses with complete grammatical analysis. The full text of all 66 verses follows in Part IV."],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"Adhyāya 1, §3, verse 1","title":"The Eight Āsanas Enumerated","sa":["स्वस्तिकगोमुखपद्मवीरसिंहभद्रमुक्तमयूराख्यान्यासनान्यष्टौ ।"],"iast":["svastika-gomukha-padma-vīra-siṃha-bhadra-mukta-mayūrākhyāny āsanāny aṣṭau |"],"words":[["svastika","m.","svastika (auspicious)"],["gomukha","m.","gomukha (cow-face)"],["padma","m.","padma (lotus)"],["vīra","m.","vīra (hero)"],["siṃha","m.","siṃha (lion)"],["bhadra","m.","bhadra (auspicious)"],["mukta","m.","mukta (liberated/free)"],["mayūra","m.","mayūra (peacock)"],["ākhyāni","cmpd. n. nom. pl.","so-named"],["āsanāni","n. nom. pl.","āsanas / postures"],["aṣṭau","numeral nom.","eight"]],"lit":"The eight āsanas (postures) are named: Svastika, Gomukha, Padma, Vīra, Siṃha, Bhadra, Mukta, and Mayūra.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The opening enumeration of the eight āsanas. Notice the dvandva (copulative) compound joining all eight names into a single nominal head, which then takes \"āsanāny aṣṭau\" as the predicate. The first 8 are juxtaposed as one collective noun."]}]},{"t":"","u":[{"ref":"Adhyāya 1, §3, verse 3","title":"Padmāsana","sa":["ऊर्वोरुपरि शाण्डिल्य कृत्वा पादतले उभे ।","पद्मासनं भवेदेतत्सर्वेषामपि पूजितम् ॥"],"iast":["ūrvor upari śāṇḍilya kṛtvā pādatale ubhe |","padmāsanaṃ bhaved etat sarveṣām api pūjitam ||"],"words":[["ūrvoḥ","m. loc. du.","on the two thighs"],["upari","adv.","above / upon"],["śāṇḍilya","voc. sg.","O Śāṇḍilya"],["kṛtvā","gerund","having placed"],["pādatale","n. acc. du.","the two soles of the feet"],["ubhe","n. acc. du.","both"],["padmāsanam","n. nom. sg.","padmāsana (lotus posture)"],["bhavet","3rd sg. opt.","becomes / would be"],["etat","n. nom. sg.","this"],["sarveṣām","gen. pl.","of all"],["api","particle","indeed / also"],["pūjitam","p.p. n. nom. sg.","worshipped / revered"]],"lit":"Having placed both soles of the feet upon the thighs, O Śāṇḍilya — this becomes Padmāsana, revered by all.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The classical lotus posture. The construction \"ūrvor upari... pādatale ubhe\" specifies that both feet go on the opposing thighs — the full padma, not the half. The vocative \"śāṇḍilya\" addresses the sage directly within the text, emphasizing the personal teaching context."]},{"ref":"Adhyāya 1, §3, verse 7","title":"Siddhāsana","sa":["योनीं वामेन सम्पीड्य मेढ्राद्रुपरि दक्षिणम् ।","भ्रूमध्ये च मनोलक्ष्यं सिद्धासनमिदं भवेत् ॥"],"iast":["yonīṃ vāmena sampīḍya meḍhrād upari dakṣiṇam |","bhrūmadhye ca mano-lakṣyaṃ siddhāsanam idaṃ bhavet ||"],"words":[["yonīm","f. acc. sg.","the perineum"],["vāmena","m. instr. sg.","with the left [foot]"],["sampīḍya","gerund","having pressed"],["meḍhrāt","n. abl. sg.","from the genitals"],["upari","adv.","above"],["dakṣiṇam","m. acc. sg.","the right [foot]"],["bhrū-madhye","n. loc. sg.","between the brows"],["ca","particle","and"],["manaḥ-lakṣyam","cmpd. n. nom. sg.","mind-aim / mental focus"],["siddhāsanam","n. nom. sg.","siddhāsana (the perfect posture)"],["idam","n. nom. sg.","this"]],"lit":"Pressing the perineum with the left [heel], placing the right [foot] above the genitals, with mental focus between the brows — this becomes Siddhāsana.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Siddhāsana — \"the perfect posture\" — is the meditation pose par excellence. The text gives the precise mechanics: left heel to perineum, right foot above the genitals (resting on the left thigh near the root), and the mind's gaze fixed at the brow-center (the ājñā cakra). This combines body, breath, and mind in a single stable configuration."]},{"ref":"Adhyāya 1, §3, verse 11","title":"Mayūrāsana","sa":["समुन्नतशिरःपादो दण्डवद्व्योम्नि संस्थितः ।","मयूरासनमेतत्तु सर्वपापप्रणाशनम् ॥"],"iast":["samunnata-śiraḥ-pādo daṇḍavad vyomni saṃsthitaḥ |","mayūrāsanam etat tu sarva-pāpa-praṇāśanam ||"],"words":[["samunnata-śiraḥ-pādaḥ","cmpd. m. nom. sg.","with head and feet raised"],["daṇḍa-vat","adv.","like a staff"],["vyomni","n. loc. sg.","in the sky / in space"],["saṃsthitaḥ","p.p. m. nom. sg.","established / standing"],["mayūrāsanam","n. nom. sg.","Mayūrāsana (peacock pose)"],["etat","n. nom. sg.","this"],["tu","particle","indeed"],["sarva-pāpa-praṇāśanam","cmpd. n. nom. sg.","destroyer of all sins"]],"lit":"With head and feet raised, standing like a staff in the air — this is Mayūrāsana, destroyer of all sins.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The peacock pose — body held horizontal in mid-air, supported on the elbows pressed against the navel. Of the eight āsanas, only this one is non-seated. Its inclusion shows the early Yoga Upaniṣadic tradition was already developing the muscular postures that Haṭha-Yoga would later expand into hundreds. The claim \"destroyer of all sins\" reflects the early association of strenuous postures with purification (tapas)."]},{"ref":"Adhyāya 1, §7, verse 11","title":"The Manonmanī State","sa":["मारुते मध्यसञ्चारे मनःस्थैर्यं प्रजायते ।","यो मनःसुस्थिरो भावः सैवावस्था मनोन्मनी ॥"],"iast":["mārute madhya-sañcāre manaḥ-sthairyaṃ prajāyate |","yo manaḥ-susthiro bhāvaḥ saivāvasthā manonmanī ||"],"words":[["mārute","m. loc. sg.","when the wind / breath"],["madhya-sañcāre","cmpd. m. loc. sg.","in the middle-moving (i.e., in Suṣumnā)"],["manaḥ-sthairyam","cmpd. n. nom. sg.","steadiness of mind"],["prajāyate","3rd sg. pres.","arises / is born"],["yaḥ","rel. m. nom. sg.","which"],["manaḥ-susthiraḥ","cmpd. m. nom. sg.","well-steadied of mind"],["bhāvaḥ","m. nom. sg.","state / condition"],["sā eva avasthā","—","that very state"],["manonmanī","f. nom. sg.","manonmanī (super-mental)"]],"lit":"When the breath moves in the middle (Suṣumnā), steadiness of mind arises. That very state of well-steadied mind is the manonmanī state.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["A key technical definition. Manonmanī (\"the supra-mental\") is the state beyond ordinary mind — where mind itself has become \"un-mind\" (un-manī). The text precisely correlates: when breath enters Suṣumnā, mind steadies; the steady-mind state IS manonmanī. This is the same state called amanaska in other Haṭha-Yoga texts."]},{"ref":"Adhyāya 1, §7, verse 15","title":"The Vaiṣṇavī Mudrā","sa":["अन्तर्लक्ष्यं बहिर्दृष्टिर्निमेषोन्मेषवर्जिता ।","एषा सा वैष्णवी मुद्रा सर्वतन्त्रेषु गोपिता ॥"],"iast":["antar-lakṣyaṃ bahir-dṛṣṭir nimeṣa-unmeṣa-varjitā |","eṣā sā vaiṣṇavī mudrā sarva-tantreṣu gopitā ||"],"words":[["antaḥ-lakṣyam","cmpd. n. nom. sg.","inner aim / target within"],["bahiḥ-dṛṣṭiḥ","cmpd. f. nom. sg.","outer gaze"],["nimeṣa-unmeṣa-varjitā","cmpd. f. nom. sg.","free from closing-and-opening (of eyes)"],["eṣā","f. nom. sg.","this"],["sā","f. nom. sg.","that"],["vaiṣṇavī mudrā","f. nom. sg.","Vaiṣṇavī Mudrā"],["sarva-tantreṣu","cmpd. loc. pl.","in all Tantras"],["gopitā","p.p. f. nom. sg.","kept secret"]],"lit":"With inner aim and outer gaze, free from blinking — this is the Vaiṣṇavī Mudrā, kept secret in all Tantras.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["<strong>Note.</strong> This is the same mudrā that the Vijñāna Bhairava Tantra v.80 names \"Bhairavī Mudrā.\" Different traditions name it differently (Vaiṣṇavī here, Bhairavī in Śaiva texts, Khecarī in others), but the practice is identical: eyes open outward, awareness turned inward, no blinking. The repeated description across multiple Upaniṣads and Tantras testifies to its centrality."]},{"ref":"Adhyāya 1, §7, verse 22","title":"Beyond Inner and Outer Thought","sa":["बाह्यचिन्ता न कर्तव्या तथैवान्तरचिन्तिका ।","सर्वचिन्तां परित्यज्य चिन्मात्रपरमो भव ॥"],"iast":["bāhya-cintā na kartavyā tathaivāntara-cintikā |","sarva-cintāṃ parityajya cinmātra-paramo bhava ||"],"words":[["bāhya-cintā","cmpd. f. nom. sg.","outer thought"],["na kartavyā","neg. + gerundive","should not be made"],["tathā eva","adv.","likewise"],["āntara-cintikā","f. nom. sg.","inner thought"],["sarva-cintām","f. acc. sg.","all thought"],["parityajya","gerund","having abandoned"],["cit-mātra-paramaḥ","cmpd. m. nom. sg.","absorbed solely in pure consciousness"],["bhava","2nd sg. imper.","become / be"]],"lit":"Outer thought should not be made, nor likewise inner thought. Abandoning all thought, become absorbed in pure consciousness alone.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["A direct instruction in the practice of cit-mātra — pure consciousness. Most meditation traditions emphasize letting go of outer objects; the Śāṇḍilya is precise that inner thought must equally be released. What remains, when both are dropped, is \"cinmātra\" — consciousness only, without object."]},{"ref":"Adhyāya 1, §7, verse 23","title":"The Mind Dissolves","sa":["कर्पूरमनले यद्वत्सैन्धवं सलिले यथा ।","तथा च लीयमानं च मनस्तत्त्वे विलीयते ॥"],"iast":["karpūram anale yadvat saindhavaṃ salile yathā |","tathā ca līyamānaṃ ca manas tattve vilīyate ||"],"words":[["karpūram","n. nom. sg.","camphor"],["anale","m. loc. sg.","in fire"],["yadvat","particle","just as"],["saindhavam","n. nom. sg.","rock-salt"],["salile","n. loc. sg.","in water"],["yathā","particle","just as"],["tathā","adv.","so"],["līyamānam","pres. part. n. nom. sg.","dissolving"],["manaḥ","n. nom. sg.","mind"],["tattve","n. loc. sg.","in the Tattva (essence)"],["vilīyate","3rd sg. pres. pass.","is dissolved / merges"]],"lit":"Just as camphor in fire, as rock-salt in water — so the mind, dissolving, merges into the Tattva.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Two of the most beloved analogies in Indian yogic literature. Camphor vanishes entirely when burned — leaving no residue. Salt fully dissolves into water — invisible but suffusing the whole. The mind that has dissolved into Brahman is not destroyed; it is absorbed without remainder, fully merged into the One."]},{"ref":"Adhyāya 1, §7, verse 24","title":"Knowledge Defined","sa":["ज्ञेयं सर्वप्रतीतं च तज्ज्ञानं मन उच्यते ।","ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं समं नष्टं नान्यः पन्था द्वितीयकः ॥"],"iast":["jñeyaṃ sarva-pratītaṃ ca taj jñānaṃ mana ucyate |","jñānaṃ jñeyaṃ samaṃ naṣṭaṃ nānyaḥ panthā dvitīyakaḥ ||"],"words":[["jñeyam","n. nom. sg.","the knowable"],["sarva-pratītam","cmpd. n. nom. sg.","all cognized"],["ca","particle","and"],["tat jñānam","n. nom. sg.","that knowledge"],["manaḥ","n. nom. sg.","mind"],["ucyate","3rd sg. pres. pass.","is called"],["samam","adv.","equally / together"],["naṣṭam","p.p. n. nom. sg.","destroyed"],["na anyaḥ","neg. + m. nom. sg.","no other"],["panthāḥ","m. nom. sg.","path"],["dvitīyakaḥ","m. nom. sg.","second"]],"lit":"The knowable, all that is cognized, and that knowledge — these together are called Mind. When the knowable, the knower, and knowing are equally destroyed — there is no other, no second path.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["A profound philosophical statement. Mind is named the composite of three: the knower (subject), the knowable (object), and the act of knowing. When these three (the tri-puṭī) are destroyed equally, what remains is Brahman. The text emphasizes \"no other path\" — only the simultaneous dissolution of the three liberates."]},{"ref":"Adhyāya 1, §7, verse 26","title":"The Two Means","sa":["द्वौ क्रमौ चित्तनाशस्य योगो ज्ञानं मुनीश्वर ।","योगस्तद्वृत्तिरोधो हि ज्ञानं सम्यगवेक्षणम् ॥"],"iast":["dvau kramau citta-nāśasya yogo jñānaṃ munīśvara |","yogas tad-vṛtti-rodho hi jñānaṃ samyag-avekṣaṇam ||"],"words":[["dvau kramau","m. nom. du.","two means"],["citta-nāśasya","cmpd. m. gen. sg.","of the destruction of citta"],["yogaḥ","m. nom. sg.","Yoga"],["jñānam","n. nom. sg.","Knowledge"],["muni-īśvara","voc. sg.","O lord of sages"],["tat-vṛtti-rodhaḥ","cmpd. m. nom. sg.","restraint of its (mind's) modifications"],["hi","particle","indeed"],["samyak-avekṣaṇam","cmpd. n. nom. sg.","right discernment"]],"lit":"Two are the means of destruction of mind, O lord of sages: Yoga and Knowledge. Yoga is the restraint of mind's modifications. Knowledge is right discernment.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["A precise definitional statement. \"Yoga = citta-vṛtti-nirodha\" is the famous formula of Yoga Sūtras 1.2 — here Śāṇḍilya echoes it. But adds: Knowledge (jñāna) is samyag-avekṣaṇa — right discernment — the complementary means. Yoga calms the mind by practice; Knowledge dissolves it by insight. Both work."]},{"ref":"Adhyāya 1, §10","title":"Definition of Dhyāna","sa":["अथ ध्यानम् । तद्द्विविधं सगुणं निर्गुणं चेति ।","सगुणं मूर्तिध्यानम् । निर्गुणमात्मयाथात्म्यम् ।"],"iast":["atha dhyānam | tad-dvividhaṃ saguṇaṃ nirguṇaṃ ceti |","saguṇaṃ mūrti-dhyānam | nirguṇam ātma-yāthātmyam |"],"words":[["atha","particle","now"],["dhyānam","n. nom. sg.","meditation"],["tat-dvividham","cmpd. n. nom. sg.","it [is] twofold"],["sa-guṇam","n. nom. sg.","with qualities"],["nirguṇam","n. nom. sg.","without qualities"],["ca iti","particle","and thus"],["mūrti-dhyānam","cmpd. n. nom. sg.","meditation on form"],["ātma-yāthātmyam","cmpd. n. nom. sg.","the actuality of the Self"]],"lit":"Now, dhyāna (meditation). It is twofold: with qualities (saguṇa) and without qualities (nirguṇa). Saguṇa is meditation on a form. Nirguṇa is the actuality-as-it-is of the Self.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The classical Vedānta distinction. Saguṇa dhyāna takes a form (mūrti) — a deity, an image, a symbol. Nirguṇa dhyāna takes no object — it is direct recognition of the Self's own nature. Both are valid; both lead to samādhi. Most practitioners begin with saguṇa and mature into nirguṇa."]},{"ref":"Adhyāya 1, §11","title":"Definition of Samādhi","sa":["अथ समाधिः । जीवात्मपरमात्मैक्यावस्थात्रिपुटीरहिता","परमानन्दस्वरूपा शुद्धचैतन्यात्मिका भवति ।"],"iast":["atha samādhiḥ | jīvātma-paramātma-aikya-avasthā-triputī-rahitā","paramānanda-svarūpā śuddha-caitanyātmikā bhavati |"],"words":[["atha","particle","now"],["samādhiḥ","m. nom. sg.","samādhi"],["jīvātma-paramātma-aikya","cmpd.","the unity of individual-Self and supreme-Self"],["avasthā","f. nom. sg.","state"],["triputī-rahitā","cmpd. f. nom. sg.","free from the triad (knower-known-knowing)"],["paramānanda-svarūpā","cmpd. f. nom. sg.","of the form of supreme bliss"],["śuddha-caitanya-ātmikā","cmpd. f. nom. sg.","of the nature of pure consciousness"],["bhavati","3rd sg. pres.","is / becomes"]],"lit":"Now, samādhi. It is the state of union of the individual self and the supreme Self, free from the triad (knower, known, knowing) — of the form of supreme bliss, of the nature of pure consciousness.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The crowning definition of samādhi. Note the precision: it is not merely \"concentration\" but specifically the dissolution of the tri-puṭī (the threefold structure of cognition) into the unity of the two ātmans — and the resulting state has a specific quality: paramānanda (supreme bliss) and śuddha-caitanya (pure consciousness). This same definition is preserved verbatim in many later Vedānta texts."]},{"ref":"Opening Invocation","title":"","sa":["शाण्डिल्योपनिषत्प्रोक्तयमाद्यष्टाङ्गयोगिनः ।","यद्बोधाद्यान्ति कैवल्यं स रामो मे परा गतिः ॥","ॐ भद्रं कर्णेभिः श्रुणुयाम देवा भद्रं पश्येमाक्षभिर्यजत्राः ।","स्थिरैरङ्गैस्तुष्टुवा{\\म्+}सस्तनूभिर्व्यशेम देवहितं यदायुः ॥","स्वस्ति न इन्द्रो वृद्धश्रवाः स्वस्ति नः पूषा विश्ववेदाः ।","स्वस्ति नस्तार्क्ष्यो अरिष्टनेमिः स्वस्ति नो बृहस्पतिर्दधातु ॥","ॐ शान्तिः शान्तिः शान्तिः ॥"],"iast":["śāṇḍilyopaniṣatproktayamādyaṣṭāṅgayoginaḥ |","yadbodhādyānti kaivalyaṃ sa rāmo me parā gatiḥ ||","oṃ bhadraṃ karṇebhiḥ śruṇuyāma devā bhadraṃ paśyemākṣabhiryajatrāḥ |","sthirairaṅgaistuṣṭuvā{\\m+}sastanūbhirvyaśema devahitaṃ yadāyuḥ ||","svasti na indro vṛddhaśravāḥ svasti naḥ pūṣā viśvavedāḥ |","svasti nastārkṣyo ariṣṭanemiḥ svasti no bṛhaspatirdadhātu ||","oṃ śāntiḥ śāntiḥ śāntiḥ ||"],"words":[],"lit":"[Maṅgalācaraṇa:] \"I bow to Rāma whose grace gives rise to yogic-power and kaivalya — the Vaiṣṇava Yoga-Tattva — the highest goal.\"<br><br>[Śānti Mantra:] \"OM. May we hear what is auspicious through our ears, O Devas; may we see what is auspicious through our eyes, O worshipful ones. May we, sound of limb, body-firmly-praising, attain the life ordained by the Devas. May Indra of great fame bless us; may all-knowing Pūṣan bless us; may Tārkṣya, of unhindered wheel, bless us; may Bṛhaspati grant us welfare. OM. Peace. Peace. Peace.\"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]}]},{"t":"Adhyāya 1 — The Eight Limbs of Yoga","u":[{"ref":"§1","title":"The Ten Yamas","sa":["शाण्डिल्यो ह वा अथर्वाणं पप्रच्छात्मलाभोपायभूतमष्टाङ्गयोगमनुब्रूहीति । स होवाचाथर्वा यमनियमासनप्राणायामप्रत्याहारधारणाध्यानसमाधयोऽष्टाङ्गानि । तत्र दश यमाः । तथा नियमाः । आसनान्यष्टौ । त्रयःप्राणायामाः । पञ्चप्रत्याहाराः । तथा धारणा । द्विप्रकारं ध्यानम् । समाधिस्त्वेकरूपः । तत्राहिंसासत्यास्तेयब्रह्मचर्यदयाजपक्षमाधृतिमिताहारशौचानि चेति यमादश । तत्र हिंसा नाम मनोवाक्कायकर्मभिः सर्वभूतेषु सर्वदा क्लेशजननम् । सत्यं नाम मनोवाक्कायकर्मभिर्भूतहितयथार्थाभिभाषणम् । अस्तेयं नाम मनोवाक्कायकर्मभिः परद्रव्येषु निःस्पृहा । ब्रह्मचर्यं नाम सर्वावस्थासु मनोवाक्कायकर्मभिः सर्वत्र मैथुनत्यागः । दया नाम सर्वभूतेषु सर्वत्रानुग्रहः । आर्जवं नाम मनोवाक्कायकर्मणां विहिताविहितेषु जनेषु प्रवृत्तौ निवृत्तौ वा एकरूपत्वम् । क्षमा नाम प्रियाप्रियेषु सर्वेषु ताडनपूजनेषु सहनम् । धृतिर्नामार्थहानौ स्वेष्टबन्धुवियोगे तत्प्राप्तौ सर्वत्र चेतः स्थापनम् । मिताहारो नाम चतुर्थांशावशेषकसुस्निग्धमधुराहारः । शौचं नाम द्विविधं बाह्यमान्तरं चेति । तत्र मृज्जलाभ्यां बाह्यम् । मनःशुद्धिरान्तरम् । तदध्यात्मविद्यया लभ्यम्"],"iast":["śāṇḍilyo ha vā atharvāṇaṃ papracchātmalābhopāyabhūtamaṣṭāṅgayogamanubrūhīti | sa hovācātharvā yamaniyamāsanaprāṇāyāmapratyāhāradhāraṇādhyānasamādhayo'ṣṭāṅgāni | tatra daśa yamāḥ | tathā niyamāḥ | āsanānyaṣṭau | trayaḥprāṇāyāmāḥ | pañcapratyāhārāḥ | tathā dhāraṇā | dviprakāraṃ dhyānam | samādhistvekarūpaḥ | tatrāhiṃsāsatyāsteyabrahmacaryadayājapakṣamādhṛtimitāhāraśaucāni ceti yamādaśa | tatra hiṃsā nāma manovākkāyakarmabhiḥ sarvabhūteṣu sarvadā kleśajananam | satyaṃ nāma manovākkāyakarmabhirbhūtahitayathārthābhibhāṣaṇam | asteyaṃ nāma manovākkāyakarmabhiḥ paradravyeṣu niḥspṛhā | brahmacaryaṃ nāma sarvāvasthāsu manovākkāyakarmabhiḥ sarvatra maithunatyāgaḥ | dayā nāma sarvabhūteṣu sarvatrānugrahaḥ | ārjavaṃ nāma manovākkāyakarmaṇāṃ vihitāvihiteṣu janeṣu pravṛttau nivṛttau vā ekarūpatvam | kṣamā nāma priyāpriyeṣu sarveṣu tāḍanapūjaneṣu sahanam | dhṛtirnāmārthahānau sveṣṭabandhuviyoge tatprāptau sarvatra cetaḥ sthāpanam | mitāhāro nāma caturthāṃśāvaśeṣakasusnigdhamadhurāhāraḥ | śaucaṃ nāma dvividhaṃ bāhyamāntaraṃ ceti | tatra mṛjjalābhyāṃ bāhyam | manaḥśuddhirāntaram | tadadhyātmavidyayā labhyam"],"words":[],"lit":"Śāṇḍilya asked Atharvan: \"Teach me the eightfold yoga, the means of attaining the Self.\" Atharvan said: \"The eight limbs are: Yama, Niyama, Āsana, Prāṇāyāma, Pratyāhāra, Dhāraṇā, Dhyāna, and Samādhi. Among these, the Yamas are ten: ahiṃsā (non-violence), satya (truth), asteya (non-stealing), brahmacarya (celibacy), dayā (compassion), ārjava (uprightness), kṣamā (forbearance), dhṛti (steadiness), mitāhāra (moderation in food), and śauca (purity).<br><br>Ahiṃsā: not causing pain to any being at any time through mind, speech, or body. Satya: speech that conforms to reality and is beneficial to beings, through mind, speech, and body. Asteya: freedom from desire for others' property, through mind, speech, and body. Brahmacarya: abstention from sexual contact in all conditions, through mind, speech, and body, everywhere. Dayā: compassion toward all beings everywhere. Ārjava: uniformity of action — mental, verbal, and bodily — toward those engaged in prescribed or forbidden acts. Kṣamā: bearing patiently all things pleasant and unpleasant, beatings or honor. Dhṛti: keeping the mind steady in the loss of wealth, in separation from loved ones, and in their attainment alike. Mitāhāra: taking soft, sweet food while leaving one-fourth of the stomach empty. Śauca: of two kinds, external and internal. External by earth and water; internal by purity of mind — attained through Self-knowledge.\"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§2","title":"The Ten Niyamas","sa":["तपःसन्तोषास्तिक्यदानेश्वरपूजनसिद्धान्तश्रवणह्रीमतिजपो व्रतानि दश नियमाः । तत्र तपो नाम विध्युक्तकृच्छ्रचान्द्रायणादिभिः शरीरशोषणम् । सन्तोषो नाम यदृच्छालाभसन्तुष्टिः । आस्तिक्यं नाम वेदोक्तधर्माधर्मेषु विश्वासः । दानं नाम न्यायार्जितस्य धनधान्यादिः श्रद्धयार्ह्तिभ्यः प्रदानम् । ईश्वरपूजनं नाम प्रसन्नस्वभावेन यथाशक्ति विष्णुरुद्रादि पूजनम् । सिद्धान्तश्रवणं नाम वेदान्तार्थविचारः । ह्रीर्नाम वेदलौकिकमार्गकुत्सितकर्मणि लज्जा । मतिर्नाम वेदविहितकर्ममार्गेषु श्रद्धा । जपो नाम विधिवद्गुरूपदिष्टवेदाविरुद्धमन्त्राभ्यासः । तद्द्विविधं वाचिकं मानसं चेति । मानसं तु मनसा ध्यानयुक्तम् । वाचिकं द्विविधमुच्चैरुपांशुभेदेन । उच्चैरुच्चारणं यथोक्तफलम् । उपांशु सहस्रगुणम् । मानसं कोटिगुणम् । व्रतं नाम वेदोक्तविधिनिषेधानुष्ठाननैयत्यम्"],"iast":["tapaḥsantoṣāstikyadāneśvarapūjanasiddhāntaśravaṇahrīmatijapo vratāni daśa niyamāḥ | tatra tapo nāma vidhyuktakṛcchracāndrāyaṇādibhiḥ śarīraśoṣaṇam | santoṣo nāma yadṛcchālābhasantuṣṭiḥ | āstikyaṃ nāma vedoktadharmādharmeṣu viśvāsaḥ | dānaṃ nāma nyāyārjitasya dhanadhānyādiḥ śraddhayārhtibhyaḥ pradānam | īśvarapūjanaṃ nāma prasannasvabhāvena yathāśakti viṣṇurudrādi pūjanam | siddhāntaśravaṇaṃ nāma vedāntārthavicāraḥ | hrīrnāma vedalaukikamārgakutsitakarmaṇi lajjā | matirnāma vedavihitakarmamārgeṣu śraddhā | japo nāma vidhivadgurūpadiṣṭavedāviruddhamantrābhyāsaḥ | taddvividhaṃ vācikaṃ mānasaṃ ceti | mānasaṃ tu manasā dhyānayuktam | vācikaṃ dvividhamuccairupāṃśubhedena | uccairuccāraṇaṃ yathoktaphalam | upāṃśu sahasraguṇam | mānasaṃ koṭiguṇam | vrataṃ nāma vedoktavidhiniṣedhānuṣṭhānanaiyatyam"],"words":[],"lit":"The ten Niyamas are: tapas (austerity), santoṣa (contentment), āstikya (faith), dāna (charity), Īśvara-pūjana (worship of the Lord), siddhānta-śravaṇa (study of conclusive doctrine), hrī (modesty), mati (good understanding), japa (mantra-repetition), and vrata (sacred vow).<br><br>Tapas: emaciation of the body through prescribed austerities such as kṛcchra and cāndrāyaṇa. Santoṣa: satisfaction with whatever comes by itself. Āstikya: faith in the Vedic teachings on dharma and adharma. Dāna: giving rightly-earned wealth, grain, etc., with faith to deserving recipients. Īśvara-pūjana: worship of Viṣṇu, Rudra, etc., to the best of capacity, with a pleased disposition. Siddhānta-śravaṇa: inquiry into the meaning of the Vedānta. Hrī: shame at performing acts contrary to Vedic and worldly path. Mati: firm conviction in the Vedic course of action. Japa: repetition of mantras as taught by the guru, not contrary to the Veda. It is twofold: verbal and mental. Mental is conjoined with meditation. Verbal is twofold: loud and whispered. Loud gives the result as stated; whispered gives a thousand-fold; mental gives a crore-fold (10 million times). Vrata: regularity in performing prescribed actions and avoiding prohibited ones.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]}]},{"t":"§3 — The Eight Āsanas (11 verses + close)","u":[{"ref":"§3 · 1","title":"","sa":["स्वस्तिकगोमुखपद्मवीरसिंहभद्रमुक्तमयूराख्यान्यासनान्यष्टौ ।","स्वस्तिकं नाम\\-जानूर्वोन्तरे सम्यक्कृत्वा पादतले उभे ।","ऋजुकायः समासीनः स्वस्तिकं तत्प्रचक्षते"],"iast":["svastikagomukhapadmavīrasiṃhabhadramuktamayūrākhyānyāsanānyaṣṭau |","svastikaṃ nāma\\-jānūrvontare samyakkṛtvā pādatale ubhe |","ṛjukāyaḥ samāsīnaḥ svastikaṃ tatpracakṣate"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§3 · 2","title":"","sa":["सव्ये दक्षिणगुल्फं तु पृष्ठपार्श्वे नियोजयेत् ।","दक्षिणेऽपि तथा सव्यं गोमुखं गोमुखं यथा"],"iast":["savye dakṣiṇagulphaṃ tu pṛṣṭhapārśve niyojayet |","dakṣiṇe'pi tathā savyaṃ gomukhaṃ gomukhaṃ yathā"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§3 · 3","title":"","sa":["अङ्गुष्ठेन निबध्नीयाद्धस्ताभ्यां व्युत्क्रमेण च ।","ऊर्वोरुपरि शाण्डिल्य कृत्वा पादतले उभे ।","पद्मासनं भवेदेतत्सर्वेषामपि पूजितम्"],"iast":["aṅguṣṭhena nibadhnīyāddhastābhyāṃ vyutkrameṇa ca |","ūrvorupari śāṇḍilya kṛtvā pādatale ubhe |","padmāsanaṃ bhavedetatsarveṣāmapi pūjitam"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§3 · 4","title":"","sa":["एकं पादमथैकस्मिन्विन्यस्योरुणि संस्थितः ।","इतरस्मिंस्तथा चोरूं वीरासनमुदीरितम्"],"iast":["ekaṃ pādamathaikasminvinyasyoruṇi saṃsthitaḥ |","itarasmiṃstathā corūṃ vīrāsanamudīritam"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§3 · 5","title":"","sa":["दक्षिणं सव्यगुल्फेन दक्षिणेन तथेतरम् ।","हस्तौ च जान्वोः संस्थाप्य स्वाङ्गुलीश्च प्रसार्य च"],"iast":["dakṣiṇaṃ savyagulphena dakṣiṇena tathetaram |","hastau ca jānvoḥ saṃsthāpya svāṅgulīśca prasārya ca"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§3 · 6","title":"","sa":["व्यक्तवक्त्रो निरीक्षेत नासाग्रं सुसमाहितः ।","सिंहासनं भवेदेतत्पूजितं योगिभिः सदा"],"iast":["vyaktavaktro nirīkṣeta nāsāgraṃ susamāhitaḥ |","siṃhāsanaṃ bhavedetatpūjitaṃ yogibhiḥ sadā"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§3 · 7","title":"","sa":["योनीं वामेन सम्पीड्य मेढ्राद्रुपरि दक्षिणम् ।","भ्रूमध्ये च मनोलक्ष्यं सिद्धासनमिदं भवेत्"],"iast":["yonīṃ vāmena sampīḍya meḍhrādrupari dakṣiṇam |","bhrūmadhye ca manolakṣyaṃ siddhāsanamidaṃ bhavet"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§3 · 8","title":"","sa":["गुल्फौ तु वृषणस्याधः सीवन्याः पार्श्वयोः क्षिपेत् ।","पादपार्श्वे तु पाणिभ्यां दृढं बध्वा सुनिश्चलम् ।","भद्रासनं भवेदेतत्सर्वव्याधिविषापहम्"],"iast":["gulphau tu vṛṣaṇasyādhaḥ sīvanyāḥ pārśvayoḥ kṣipet |","pādapārśve tu pāṇibhyāṃ dṛḍhaṃ badhvā suniścalam |","bhadrāsanaṃ bhavedetatsarvavyādhiviṣāpaham"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§3 · 9","title":"","sa":["सम्पीड्य सीविनीं सूक्ष्मां गुल्फेनैव तु सव्यतः ।","सव्यं दक्षिणगुल्फेन मुक्तासनमुदीरितम्"],"iast":["sampīḍya sīvinīṃ sūkṣmāṃ gulphenaiva tu savyataḥ |","savyaṃ dakṣiṇagulphena muktāsanamudīritam"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§3 · 10","title":"","sa":["अवष्टभ्य धरां सम्यक्तलाभ्यां तु करद्वयोः ।","हस्तयोः कूर्परौ चापि स्थापयेन्नाभिपार्श्वयओः"],"iast":["avaṣṭabhya dharāṃ samyaktalābhyāṃ tu karadvayoḥ |","hastayoḥ kūrparau cāpi sthāpayennābhipārśvayaoḥ"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§3 · 11","title":"","sa":["समुन्नतशिरःपादो दण्डवद्व्योम्नि संस्थितः ।","मयूरासनमेतत्तु सर्वपापप्रणाशनम्","शरीरान्तर्गताः सर्वे रोगा विनश्यन्ति । विषाणि जीर्यन्ते । येन केनासनेन सुखधारणं भवत्यशक्तस्तत्समाचरेत् । येनासनं विजितं जगत्त्रयं तेन विजितं भवति । यमनियमाभ्यां संयुक्तः पुरुषः प्राणायामं चरेत् । तेन नाड्यः शुद्धा भवन्ति"],"iast":["samunnataśiraḥpādo daṇḍavadvyomni saṃsthitaḥ |","mayūrāsanametattu sarvapāpapraṇāśanam","śarīrāntargatāḥ sarve rogā vinaśyanti | viṣāṇi jīryante | yena kenāsanena sukhadhāraṇaṃ bhavatyaśaktastatsamācaret | yenāsanaṃ vijitaṃ jagattrayaṃ tena vijitaṃ bhavati | yamaniyamābhyāṃ saṃyuktaḥ puruṣaḥ prāṇāyāmaṃ caret | tena nāḍyaḥ śuddhā bhavanti"],"words":[],"lit":"Through these āsanas, all diseases within the body are destroyed and poisons are digested. He who is unable to do these should practice whatever āsana is comfortable. He who has conquered āsana has conquered the three worlds. Endowed with yama and niyama, the person should practice prāṇāyāma; by it the nāḍīs become purified.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Closing prose of §3:"]}]},{"t":"","u":[{"ref":"§4","title":"The 14 Nāḍīs and 10 Vāyus","sa":["अथ हैनमथर्वाणं शाण्डिल्यः पप्रच्छ केनोपायेन नाड्यः शुद्धाः स्युः । नाड्यः कतिसंख्याकाः । तासामुत्पत्तिः कीदृशी । तासु कति वयवस्तिष्ठन्ति । तेषां कानि स्थानानि । तत्कर्माणि कानि । देहे यानि यानि विज्ञातव्यानि तत्सर्वं मे ब्रूहीति । स होवाच अथर्वाण अथेदं शरीरं षण्णवत्यङ्गुलात्मकं भवति । शरीरात्प्राणो द्वादशाङ्गुलाधिको भवति । शरीरस्थं प्राणमग्निना सह योगाभ्यासेन समं न्यूनं वा यः करोति स योगिपुङ्गवो भवति । देहमध्ये शिखिस्थानं त्रिकोणं तप्तजाम्बूनदप्रभं मनुष्याणाम् । चतुष्पदां चतुरस्रम् । विहङ्गानां वृत्ताकारम् । तन्मध्ये शुभा तन्वी पावकी शिखा तिष्ठति । गुदाद्व्यङ्गुलादूर्ध्वं मेढ्राद्व्यङ्गुलादधो देहमध्यं मनुष्याणां भवति । चतुष्पदां हृन्मध्यम् । विहङ्गानां तुङ्गमध्यम् । देहमध्यं नवाङ्गुलं चतुरङ्गुलमुत्सेधायतमण्डाकृति । तन्मध्ये नाभिः । तत्र द्वादशारयुतं चक्रम् । तच्चक्रमध्ये पुण्यपापप्रचोदितो जीवो भ्रमति । तन्तुपञ्जरमध्यस्थलूतिका यथा भ्रमति तथा चासौ तत्र प्राणश्चरति । देहेऽस्मिञ्जीवः प्राणारूढो भवेत् । नाभेस्तिर्यगधऊर्ध्वं कुण्डलिनीस्थानम् । अष्टप्रकृतिरूपाष्टधा कुण्डलीकृता कुण्डलिनी शक्तिर्भवति । यथावद्वायुसंचारं जलान्नादीनि परितः स्कन्धः पार्श्वेषु निरुध्यैनं मुखेनैव समावेष्ट्य ब्रह्मरन्ध्रं योगकाले चापानेनाग्निना च स्फुरति । हृदयाकाशे महोज्ज्वला ज्ञानरूपा भवति ।  मध्यस्थकुण्डलिनीमाश्रित्य मुख्या नाड्यश्चतुर्दश भवन्ति । इडा पिङ्गला सुषुम्ना सरस्वती वारुणी पूषा हस्तिजिह्वा यशस्विनी विश्वोदरी कुहूः शङ्खिनी पयस्विनी अलम्बुसा गान्धारीति नाड्यचतुर्दश भवन्ति । तत्र सुषुम्ना विश्वधारिणी मोक्षमार्गेति चाचक्षते । गुदस्य पृष्ठभागे वीणादण्डाश्रिता मूर्धपर्यन्तं ब्रह्मरन्ध्रे विज्ञेया व्यक्ता सूक्ष्मा वैष्णवी भवति । सुषुम्नायाः सव्यभागे इडा तिष्ठति । दक्षिणभागे पिङ्गला इडायां चन्द्रश्चरति । पिङ्गलायां रविः । तमोरूपश्चन्द्रः । रजोरूपो रविः । विषभागो रविः । अमृतभागश्चन्द्रमाः । तावेव सर्वकालं धत्ते । सुषुम्ना कालभोक्त्री भवति । सुषुम्ना पृष्ठपार्श्वयोः सरस्वतीकुहू भवतः । यशस्विनीकुहूमध्ये वारुणी प्रतिष्ठिता भवति । पूषासरस्वतीमध्ये पयस्विनी भवति । गान्धारीसरस्वतिमध्ये यशस्विनी भवति । कन्दमयेऽलम्बुसा भवति।  सुषुम्नापूर्वभागे मेढ्रान्तं कुहूर्भवति । कुण्डलिन्या अधश्चोर्ध्वं वारुणी सर्वगामिनी भवति । यशस्विनी सौम्या च पादाङ्गुष्ठान्तमिष्यते । पिङ्गला चोर्ध्वगा याम्यनासान्तं भवति । पिङ्गलायाः पृष्ठतो याम्यनेत्रानतं पूषा भवति । याम्यकर्णान्तं यशस्विनी भवति । जिह्वाया ऊर्ध्वानतं सरस्वती भवति । आसव्यकर्णान्तमूर्ध्वगा शङ्खिनी भवति । इडापृष्ठभागात्सव्यनेत्रान्तगा गान्धारी भवति । पायुमूलादधोर्ध्वगालम्बुसा भवति । एताश्च चतुर्दशसु नाडीष्वन्या नाड्यः संभवन्ति । तास्वन्यास्तास्वन्या भवन्तीति विज्ञेयाः ॥ यथाश्वत्थादिपत्रं शिराभिर्व्याप्तमेवं शरीरं नाडीभिर्व्याप्तम् । प्राणापानसमानोदानव्याना नागकूर्मकृकरदेवदत्तधनञ्जया एते दश वायवः सर्वासु नाडीषु चरन्ति । आस्यनासिकाकण्ठनाभिपादाङ्गुष्ठद्वयकुण्डल्यधश्चोर्ध्वभागेषु प्राणः संचरति । श्रोत्राक्षिकटिगुल्फघ्राणगलस्फिग्देशेषु व्यानः संचरति । गुदमेढ्रोरुजानूदरवृषणकटिजङ्घानाभिगुदाग्न्यगारेष्वपानः संचरति । सर्वसन्धिस्थ उदानः । पादहस्तयोरपि सर्वगात्रेषु सर्वव्यापी समानः । भुक्तान्नरसादिकं गात्रेग्निना सह व्यापयन्द्विसप्ततिसहस्रेषु नाडीमार्गेषु चरन्समानवायुरग्निना सह साङ्गोपाङ्गकलेवरं व्याप्नोति । नागादिवायवः पञ्चत्वगस्थ्यादिसंभवाः । तुन्दस्थं जलमन्नं च रसादिषु समीरितं तुन्दमध्यगतः प्रागस्तानि पृथक्कुर्यात् । अग्नेरुपरि जलं स्थाप्य जलोपर्यन्नादीनि संस्थाप्य स्वयमपानं सम्प्राप्य तेनैव सह मारुतः प्रयाति देहमध्यगतं ज्वलनम् । वायुना पालितो वह्निरपानेन शनैर्देहमध्ये ज्वलति । ज्वलनो ज्वालाभिः प्राणेन कोष्ठमध्यगतं जलमत्युष्णमकरोत् । जलोपरि समर्पितव्यञ्जनसंयुक्तमन्नं वह्निसंयुक्तवारिणा पक्वमकरोत् । तेन स्वेदमूत्रजलरक्तवीर्यरूपरसपुरीषादिकं प्राणः पृथक्कुर्यात् । समानवायुना सह सर्वासु नाडीषु रसं व्यापयञ्छ्वासरूपेण देहे वायुश्चरति । नवभिर्व्योमरन्ध्रैः शरीरस्य वायवः कुर्वन्ति विण्मूत्रादिविसर्जनम् । निश्वासोच्छ्वासकासश्च प्राणकर्मोच्यते । विण्मूत्रादिविसर्जनमपानवायुकर्म । हानोपादानचेष्टादि व्यानकर्म । देहस्योन्नयनादिकमुदानकर्म । शरीरपोषणादिकं समानकर्म । उद्गारादि नागकर्म । निमीलनादि कूर्मकर्म । क्षुत्करणं कृकरकर्म । तन्द्रा देवदत्तकर्म । श्लेष्मादि धनञ्जयकर्म । एवं नाडीस्थानं वायुस्थानं तत्कर्म च सम्यग्ज्ञात्वा नाडीसंशोधनं कुर्यात्"],"iast":["atha hainamatharvāṇaṃ śāṇḍilyaḥ papraccha kenopāyena nāḍyaḥ śuddhāḥ syuḥ | nāḍyaḥ katisaṃkhyākāḥ | tāsāmutpattiḥ kīdṛśī | tāsu kati vayavastiṣṭhanti | teṣāṃ kāni sthānāni | tatkarmāṇi kāni | dehe yāni yāni vijñātavyāni tatsarvaṃ me brūhīti | sa hovāca atharvāṇa athedaṃ śarīraṃ ṣaṇṇavatyaṅgulātmakaṃ bhavati | śarīrātprāṇo dvādaśāṅgulādhiko bhavati | śarīrasthaṃ prāṇamagninā saha yogābhyāsena samaṃ nyūnaṃ vā yaḥ karoti sa yogipuṅgavo bhavati | dehamadhye śikhisthānaṃ trikoṇaṃ taptajāmbūnadaprabhaṃ manuṣyāṇām | catuṣpadāṃ caturasram | vihaṅgānāṃ vṛttākāram | tanmadhye śubhā tanvī pāvakī śikhā tiṣṭhati | gudādvyaṅgulādūrdhvaṃ meḍhrādvyaṅgulādadho dehamadhyaṃ manuṣyāṇāṃ bhavati | catuṣpadāṃ hṛnmadhyam | vihaṅgānāṃ tuṅgamadhyam | dehamadhyaṃ navāṅgulaṃ caturaṅgulamutsedhāyatamaṇḍākṛti | tanmadhye nābhiḥ | tatra dvādaśārayutaṃ cakram | taccakramadhye puṇyapāpapracodito jīvo bhramati | tantupañjaramadhyasthalūtikā yathā bhramati tathā cāsau tatra prāṇaścarati | dehe'smiñjīvaḥ prāṇārūḍho bhavet | nābhestiryagadha_ūrdhvaṃ kuṇḍalinīsthānam | aṣṭaprakṛtirūpāṣṭadhā kuṇḍalīkṛtā kuṇḍalinī śaktirbhavati | yathāvadvāyusaṃcāraṃ jalānnādīni paritaḥ skandhaḥ pārśveṣu nirudhyainaṃ mukhenaiva samāveṣṭya brahmarandhraṃ yogakāle cāpānenāgninā ca sphurati | hṛdayākāśe mahojjvalā jñānarūpā bhavati |  madhyasthakuṇḍalinīmāśritya mukhyā nāḍyaścaturdaśa bhavanti | iḍā piṅgalā suṣumnā sarasvatī vāruṇī pūṣā hastijihvā yaśasvinī viśvodarī kuhūḥ śaṅkhinī payasvinī alambusā gāndhārīti nāḍyacaturdaśa bhavanti | tatra suṣumnā viśvadhāriṇī mokṣamārgeti cācakṣate | gudasya pṛṣṭhabhāge vīṇādaṇḍāśritā mūrdhaparyantaṃ brahmarandhre vijñeyā vyaktā sūkṣmā vaiṣṇavī bhavati | suṣumnāyāḥ savyabhāge iḍā tiṣṭhati | dakṣiṇabhāge piṅgalā iḍāyāṃ candraścarati | piṅgalāyāṃ raviḥ | tamorūpaścandraḥ | rajorūpo raviḥ | viṣabhāgo raviḥ | amṛtabhāgaścandramāḥ | tāveva sarvakālaṃ dhatte | suṣumnā kālabhoktrī bhavati | suṣumnā pṛṣṭhapārśvayoḥ sarasvatīkuhū bhavataḥ | yaśasvinīkuhūmadhye vāruṇī pratiṣṭhitā bhavati | pūṣāsarasvatīmadhye payasvinī bhavati | gāndhārīsarasvatimadhye yaśasvinī bhavati | kandamaye'lambusā bhavati|  suṣumnāpūrvabhāge meḍhrāntaṃ kuhūrbhavati | kuṇḍalinyā adhaścordhvaṃ vāruṇī sarvagāminī bhavati | yaśasvinī saumyā ca pādāṅguṣṭhāntamiṣyate | piṅgalā cordhvagā yāmyanāsāntaṃ bhavati | piṅgalāyāḥ pṛṣṭhato yāmyanetrānataṃ pūṣā bhavati | yāmyakarṇāntaṃ yaśasvinī bhavati | jihvāyā ūrdhvānataṃ sarasvatī bhavati | āsavyakarṇāntamūrdhvagā śaṅkhinī bhavati | iḍāpṛṣṭhabhāgātsavyanetrāntagā gāndhārī bhavati | pāyumūlādadhordhvagālambusā bhavati | etāśca caturdaśasu nāḍīṣvanyā nāḍyaḥ saṃbhavanti | tāsvanyāstāsvanyā bhavantīti vijñeyāḥ || yathāśvatthādipatraṃ śirābhirvyāptamevaṃ śarīraṃ nāḍībhirvyāptam | prāṇāpānasamānodānavyānā nāgakūrmakṛkaradevadattadhanañjayā ete daśa vāyavaḥ sarvāsu nāḍīṣu caranti | āsyanāsikākaṇṭhanābhipādāṅguṣṭhadvayakuṇḍalyadhaścordhvabhāgeṣu prāṇaḥ saṃcarati | śrotrākṣikaṭigulphaghrāṇagalasphigdeśeṣu vyānaḥ saṃcarati | gudameḍhrorujānūdaravṛṣaṇakaṭijaṅghānābhigudāgnyagāreṣvapānaḥ saṃcarati | sarvasandhistha udānaḥ | pādahastayorapi sarvagātreṣu sarvavyāpī samānaḥ | bhuktānnarasādikaṃ gātregninā saha vyāpayandvisaptatisahasreṣu nāḍīmārgeṣu caransamānavāyuragninā saha sāṅgopāṅgakalevaraṃ vyāpnoti | nāgādivāyavaḥ pañcatvagasthyādisaṃbhavāḥ | tundasthaṃ jalamannaṃ ca rasādiṣu samīritaṃ tundamadhyagataḥ prāgastāni pṛthakkuryāt | agnerupari jalaṃ sthāpya jaloparyannādīni saṃsthāpya svayamapānaṃ samprāpya tenaiva saha mārutaḥ prayāti dehamadhyagataṃ jvalanam | vāyunā pālito vahnirapānena śanairdehamadhye jvalati | jvalano jvālābhiḥ prāṇena koṣṭhamadhyagataṃ jalamatyuṣṇamakarot | jalopari samarpitavyañjanasaṃyuktamannaṃ vahnisaṃyuktavāriṇā pakvamakarot | tena svedamūtrajalaraktavīryarūparasapurīṣādikaṃ prāṇaḥ pṛthakkuryāt | samānavāyunā saha sarvāsu nāḍīṣu rasaṃ vyāpayañchvāsarūpeṇa dehe vāyuścarati | navabhirvyomarandhraiḥ śarīrasya vāyavaḥ kurvanti viṇmūtrādivisarjanam | niśvāsocchvāsakāsaśca prāṇakarmocyate | viṇmūtrādivisarjanamapānavāyukarma | hānopādānaceṣṭādi vyānakarma | dehasyonnayanādikamudānakarma | śarīrapoṣaṇādikaṃ samānakarma | udgārādi nāgakarma | nimīlanādi kūrmakarma | kṣutkaraṇaṃ kṛkarakarma | tandrā devadattakarma | śleṣmādi dhanañjayakarma | evaṃ nāḍīsthānaṃ vāyusthānaṃ tatkarma ca samyagjñātvā nāḍīsaṃśodhanaṃ kuryāt"],"words":[],"lit":"Then Śāṇḍilya asked Atharvan: \"By what means do the nāḍīs become purified? How many nāḍīs are there? What is their origin? How many vāyus dwell in them? Where are their seats? What are their functions? Tell me everything that should be known regarding the body.\"<br><br>Atharvan replied: \"This body is 96 aṅgulas long. From the body, prāṇa extends 12 aṅgulas beyond it. He who, by yoga practice, makes the prāṇa within the body equal to or less than [the standard reach] together with the fire — he becomes the best of yogis. In the middle of the body, in human beings, is a triangular fire-place shining like molten gold. In quadrupeds it is square; in birds it is circular. Within this is a thin, bright, flame — the inner Pāvaka fire. Two aṅgulas above the anus, two aṅgulas below the genitals — that is the middle of the body in humans. In quadrupeds the heart-middle. In birds the central beak.<br><br>The middle of the body is 9 aṅgulas long, 4 aṅgulas wide, oval-shaped. In its center is the navel; there is a wheel (cakra) with twelve spokes. Within that wheel the jīva wanders, driven by merit and demerit. As a spider runs about in the web she has spun, so the prāṇa moves about there. The jīva in this body rides upon the prāṇa.<br><br>Below, across, and above the navel is the seat of Kuṇḍalinī. The Kuṇḍalinī-Śakti is of the form of eight-fold nature (aṣṭaprakṛti), coiled eight times. It restrains the movement of air and the flow of food, drink etc., remaining around them, and at the time of yoga ascends through the suṣumnā by closing the door [of brahmarandhra] with its mouth — by apāna and fire — and spreads as a great-flame in the heart-space, in the form of consciousness.<br><br>The principal nāḍīs branching from Kuṇḍalinī are fourteen: Iḍā, Piṅgalā, Suṣumnā, Sarasvatī, Vāruṇī, Pūṣā, Hastijihvā, Yaśasvinī, Viśvodarī, Kuhū, Śaṅkhinī, Payasvinī, Alambusā, and Gāndhārī.<br><br>Of these, Suṣumnā is the universal supporter (viśva-dhāriṇī) and is called the path of liberation. Behind the anus, supported on the vīṇā-staff (spinal column), extending to the head — it is to be known in the brahmarandhra as manifest, subtle, the Vaiṣṇavī. On the left of Suṣumnā is Iḍā; on the right is Piṅgalā. In Iḍā moves the moon, in Piṅgalā the sun. The moon is of the form of darkness (tamas); the sun of the form of activity (rajas). The sun is the portion of poison; the moon is the portion of nectar. They control all time. Suṣumnā is the eater of time.<br><br>[Detailed positions of all 14 nāḍīs as described in the text.]<br><br>The ten vāyus circulating in all the nāḍīs are: Prāṇa, Apāna, Samāna, Udāna, Vyāna, Nāga, Kūrma, Kṛkara, Devadatta, and Dhanañjaya. Prāṇa moves in the mouth, nostrils, throat, navel, both big toes, in the Kuṇḍalī-region below, and upward. Vyāna moves in the ears, eyes, hips, ankles, nose, throat, and buttocks. Apāna moves in the anus, genitals, thighs, knees, abdomen, scrotum, hips, shanks, navel, and the seat of digestive fire. Udāna is in all joints. Samāna is all-pervading in feet, hands, and all limbs.<br><br>The five sub-vāyus (Nāga etc.) arise from skin, bones, etc. Belching, blinking, sneezing, drowsiness, and phlegm — these are their functions respectively. Inhalation, exhalation, and cough are functions of prāṇa. Excretion is the function of apāna. Gesture and effort are functions of vyāna. Lifting up is the function of udāna. Nourishing the body is samāna's function. Having understood the seats of the nāḍīs, the seats of the vāyus, and their functions correctly, one should perform the purification of the nāḍīs.\"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§5","title":"Prāṇāyāma Preparation","sa":["यमनियमयुतः पुरुषः सर्वसङ्गविवर्जितः कृतविद्यः सत्यधर्मरतो जितक्रोधो गुरुशुश्रूषानिरतः पितृमातृविधेयः स्वाश्रमोक्तसदाचारविद्वच्छिक्षितः फलमूलोदकान्वितं तपोवनं प्राप्य रम्यदेशे ब्रह्मघोषसमन्विते स्वधर्मनिरतब्रह्मवित्समावृते फलमूलपुष्पवारिभिः सुसम्पूर्णे देवायतने नदीतीरे ग्रामे नगरे वापि सुशोभनमठं नात्युच्चनीचायतमल्पद्वारं गोमयादिलिप्तं सर्वरक्षासमन्वितं कृत्वा तत्र वेदान्तश्रवणं कुर्वन्योगं समारभेत् । आदौ विनायकं सम्पूज्य स्वेष्टदेवतां नत्वा पूर्वोक्तासने स्थित्वा प्राङ्मुख उदङ्मुखो वापि मृद्वासनेषु जितासनगतो विद्वान्समग्रीवशिरोनासाग्रदृग्भ्रूमध्ये शशभृद्बिंबं पश्यन्नेत्राभ्याममृतं पिबेत् । द्वादशमात्रया इडया वायुमापूर्योदरे स्थितं ज्वालावलीयुतं रेफबिन्दुयुक्तमग्निमण्डलयुतं ध्यायेद्रेचयेत्पिङ्गलया । पुनः पिङ्गलयापूर्य कुम्भित्वा रेचयेदिडया । त्रिचतुस्त्रिचतुःसप्तत्रिचातुर्मासपर्यन्तं त्रिसन्धिषु तदन्तरालेषु च षट्कृत्व आचरेन्नाडीशुद्धिर्भवति । ततः शरीरे लघुदीप्तिवह्निवृद्धिनादाभिव्यक्तिर्भवति"],"iast":["yamaniyamayutaḥ puruṣaḥ sarvasaṅgavivarjitaḥ kṛtavidyaḥ satyadharmarato jitakrodho guruśuśrūṣānirataḥ pitṛmātṛvidheyaḥ svāśramoktasadācāravidvacchikṣitaḥ phalamūlodakānvitaṃ tapovanaṃ prāpya ramyadeśe brahmaghoṣasamanvite svadharmaniratabrahmavitsamāvṛte phalamūlapuṣpavāribhiḥ susampūrṇe devāyatane nadītīre grāme nagare vāpi suśobhanamaṭhaṃ nātyuccanīcāyatamalpadvāraṃ gomayādiliptaṃ sarvarakṣāsamanvitaṃ kṛtvā tatra vedāntaśravaṇaṃ kurvanyogaṃ samārabhet | ādau vināyakaṃ sampūjya sveṣṭadevatāṃ natvā pūrvoktāsane sthitvā prāṅmukha udaṅmukho vāpi mṛdvāsaneṣu jitāsanagato vidvānsamagrīvaśironāsāgradṛgbhrūmadhye śaśabhṛdbiṃbaṃ paśyannetrābhyāmamṛtaṃ pibet | dvādaśamātrayā iḍayā vāyumāpūryodare sthitaṃ jvālāvalīyutaṃ rephabinduyuktamagnimaṇḍalayutaṃ dhyāyedrecayetpiṅgalayā | punaḥ piṅgalayāpūrya kumbhitvā recayediḍayā | tricatustricatuḥsaptatricāturmāsaparyantaṃ trisandhiṣu tadantarāleṣu ca ṣaṭkṛtva ācarennāḍīśuddhirbhavati | tataḥ śarīre laghudīptivahnivṛddhinādābhivyaktirbhavati"],"words":[],"lit":"A man endowed with yama and niyama, free from all attachment, learned, devoted to truth and dharma, having conquered anger, devoted to service of the guru, obedient to parents, taught in the conduct of his own āśrama — having reached a delightful tapas-grove provided with fruits, roots, and water, in a beautiful place resounding with Vedic chants, surrounded by twice-borns devoted to their own dharma and knowers of Brahman, by sacred temples filled with fruits, flowers and water — on the bank of a river, in a village or in a city, having built a fair hut neither too high nor too low nor too long, with a small door, plastered with cow-dung etc., provided with all means of protection — there, hearing Vedānta, he should begin yoga.<br><br>First, having worshipped Vināyaka and saluted the chosen deity, having seated himself in the previously-stated āsana facing east or north, on a soft seat, the wise one having conquered āsana, with neck and head erect, gaze fixed on the tip of the nose or between the brows — visualizing the disc of the moon — should drink nectar through both eyes. With twelve mātrās he should inhale air through Iḍā, [meditate upon] the agni-maṇḍala situated in the stomach, surrounded by flame-rows, joined with the bīja \"RA\" and \"bindu\" — then exhale through Piṅgalā. Again, having inhaled through Piṅgalā, retained, he should exhale through Iḍā. He should practice this for 3, 4 [months] up to a fourth year, three times daily and 6 times each — and the nāḍīs become purified. Then in the body arises lightness, brightness, increase of digestive fire, and the manifestation of nāda.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§6","title":"Prāṇāyāma — The AUM Protocol","sa":["प्राणापानसमायोगः प्राणायामो भवति । रेचकपूरककुम्भकभेदेन स त्रिविधः । ते वर्णात्मकाः । तस्मात्प्रणव एव प्राणायामः पद्माद्यासनस्थः पुमान्नासाग्रे शशभृद्बिम्बज्योत्स्नाजालवितानिताकारमूर्ती रक्ताङ्गी हंसवाहिनी दण्डहस्ता बाला गायत्री भवति । उकारमूर्तिः श्वेताङ्गी तार्क्ष्यवाहिनी युवती चक्रहस्ता सावित्री भवति । मकारमूर्तिः कृष्णाङ्गी वृषभवाहिनी वृद्धा त्रिशूलधारिणी सरस्वती भवति । अकारादित्रयाणां सर्वकारणमेकाक्षरं परंज्योतिः प्रणवं भवतीति ध्यायेत् । इडया बाह्याद्वायुमापूर्य षोडशमात्राभिरकारं चिन्तयन्पूरितं वायुं चतुःषष्टिमात्राभिः कुम्भयित्वोकारं ध्यायन्पूरितं पिङ्गलया द्वात्रिंशन्मात्रया मकारमूर्तिध्यानेनैवं क्रमेण पुनः पुनः कुर्यात्"],"iast":["prāṇāpānasamāyogaḥ prāṇāyāmo bhavati | recakapūrakakumbhakabhedena sa trividhaḥ | te varṇātmakāḥ | tasmātpraṇava eva prāṇāyāmaḥ padmādyāsanasthaḥ pumānnāsāgre śaśabhṛdbimbajyotsnājālavitānitākāramūrtī raktāṅgī haṃsavāhinī daṇḍahastā bālā gāyatrī bhavati | ukāramūrtiḥ śvetāṅgī tārkṣyavāhinī yuvatī cakrahastā sāvitrī bhavati | makāramūrtiḥ kṛṣṇāṅgī vṛṣabhavāhinī vṛddhā triśūladhāriṇī sarasvatī bhavati | akārāditrayāṇāṃ sarvakāraṇamekākṣaraṃ paraṃjyotiḥ praṇavaṃ bhavatīti dhyāyet | iḍayā bāhyādvāyumāpūrya ṣoḍaśamātrābhirakāraṃ cintayanpūritaṃ vāyuṃ catuḥṣaṣṭimātrābhiḥ kumbhayitvokāraṃ dhyāyanpūritaṃ piṅgalayā dvātriṃśanmātrayā makāramūrtidhyānenaivaṃ krameṇa punaḥ punaḥ kuryāt"],"words":[],"lit":"The union of prāṇa and apāna is prāṇāyāma. It is threefold: recaka (exhale), pūraka (inhale), kumbhaka (retention). They are of the form of letters. Therefore the praṇava (OM) alone is prāṇāyāma. Seated in padmāsana etc., the person — at the tip of the nose, with form constituted by the bimba of the moon and an expanse of moonbeams, red-limbed, riding a swan, with staff-in-hand — the young Gāyatrī is visualized. In the form of U-kāra she is white-limbed, riding Garuḍa, the maiden Sāvitrī with discus in hand. In the form of M-kāra she is black-limbed, riding the bull (Nandi), the aged Sarasvatī bearing the trident. He should meditate that the imperishable cause of these three — A, U, M — the supreme light is praṇava.<br><br>Through Iḍā filling air from outside with 16 mātrās, while contemplating A-kāra; then retaining the filled air for 64 mātrās while meditating U-kāra; then exhaling through Piṅgalā with 32 mātrās while meditating M-kāra — thus he should practice repeatedly, gradually.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]}]},{"t":"§7 — The Long Verse-Section (51 verses + saṃyama prose)","u":[{"ref":"§7","title":"The Long Verse-Section (51 verses + saṃyama prose)","sa":["अथासनदृढो योगी वशी मितहिताशनः","सुषुम्नानाडीस्थमलशोषार्थं योगी","बद्धपद्मासनो वायुं चन्द्रेणापूर्य","यथाशक्ति कुम्भयित्वा सूर्येण रेचयित्वा","पुनः सूर्येणापूर्य कुम्भयित्वा चन्द्रेण","विरेच्य यया त्यजेत्तया सम्पूर्य धारयेत् ।","तदेते श्लोका भवन्ति ।","प्राणं प्रागिडया पिबेन्नियमितं भूयोऽन्यया रेचयेत्पीत्वा पिङ्गलया समीरणमथो बद्ध्वा त्यजेद्वामया ।","सूर्याचन्द्रमसोरनेन विधिनाऽभ्यासं सदा तन्वतां","शुद्धा नाडिगणा भवन्ति यमिनां मासत्रयादूर्ध्वतः"],"iast":["athāsanadṛḍho yogī vaśī mitahitāśanaḥ","suṣumnānāḍīsthamalaśoṣārthaṃ yogī","baddhapadmāsano vāyuṃ candreṇāpūrya","yathāśakti kumbhayitvā sūryeṇa recayitvā","punaḥ sūryeṇāpūrya kumbhayitvā candreṇa","virecya yayā tyajettayā sampūrya dhārayet |","tadete ślokā bhavanti |","prāṇaṃ prāgiḍayā pibenniyamitaṃ bhūyo'nyayā recayetpītvā piṅgalayā samīraṇamatho baddhvā tyajedvāmayā |","sūryācandramasoranena vidhinā'bhyāsaṃ sadā tanvatāṃ","śuddhā nāḍigaṇā bhavanti yamināṃ māsatrayādūrdhvataḥ"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["This section contains 51 numbered verses on prāṇāyāma stages, the Vaiṣṇavī and Khecarī Mudrās, the dissolution of mind, and Khecarī-related practices. It is the heart of the practical instruction.","(§7 begins with a prose passage describing the meditative posture and breath-method, after which the verses begin. The first numbered verse occurs after the introductory prose:)"]},{"ref":"§7 · 2","title":"","sa":["प्रातर्मध्यन्दिने सायमर्धरात्रे तु कुम्भकान् ।","शनैरशीतिपर्यन्तं चतुर्वारं समभ्यसेत्"],"iast":["prātarmadhyandine sāyamardharātre tu kumbhakān |","śanairaśītiparyantaṃ caturvāraṃ samabhyaset"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 3","title":"","sa":["कनीयसि भवेत्स्वेदः कंपो भवति मध्यमे ।","उत्तिष्ठत्त्युत्तमे प्राणरोधे पद्मासनं महत्"],"iast":["kanīyasi bhavetsvedaḥ kaṃpo bhavati madhyame |","uttiṣṭhattyuttame prāṇarodhe padmāsanaṃ mahat"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 4","title":"","sa":["जलेन श्रमजातेन गात्रमर्दनमाचरेत् ।","दृढता लघुता चापि तस्य गात्रस्य जायते"],"iast":["jalena śramajātena gātramardanamācaret |","dṛḍhatā laghutā cāpi tasya gātrasya jāyate"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 5","title":"","sa":["अभ्यासकाले प्रथमं शस्तं क्षीराज्यभोजनम् ।","ततोऽभ्यासे स्थिरीभूते न तावन्नियमग्रहः"],"iast":["abhyāsakāle prathamaṃ śastaṃ kṣīrājyabhojanam |","tato'bhyāse sthirībhūte na tāvanniyamagrahaḥ"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 6","title":"","sa":["यथा सिंहो गजो व्याघ्रो भवेद्वश्यः शनैः शनैः ।","तथैव सेवितो वायुरन्यथा हन्ति साधकम्"],"iast":["yathā siṃho gajo vyāghro bhavedvaśyaḥ śanaiḥ śanaiḥ |","tathaiva sevito vāyuranyathā hanti sādhakam"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 7","title":"","sa":["युक्तं युक्तं त्यजेद्वायुं युक्तं युक्तं च पूरयेत् ।","युक्तं युक्तं च बध्नीयादेवं सिद्धिमवाप्नुयात्"],"iast":["yuktaṃ yuktaṃ tyajedvāyuṃ yuktaṃ yuktaṃ ca pūrayet |","yuktaṃ yuktaṃ ca badhnīyādevaṃ siddhimavāpnuyāt"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 8","title":"","sa":["यथेष्टधारणाद्वायोरनलस्य प्रदीपनम् ।","नादाभिव्यक्तिरारोग्यं जायते नाडिशोधनात्"],"iast":["yatheṣṭadhāraṇādvāyoranalasya pradīpanam |","nādābhivyaktirārogyaṃ jāyate nāḍiśodhanāt"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 9","title":"","sa":["विधिवत्प्राणसंयामैर्नाडीचक्रे विशोधिते ।","सुषुम्नावदनं भित्त्वा सुखाद्विशति मारुतः"],"iast":["vidhivatprāṇasaṃyāmairnāḍīcakre viśodhite |","suṣumnāvadanaṃ bhittvā sukhādviśati mārutaḥ"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 10","title":"","sa":["मारुते मध्यसंचारे मनःस्थैर्यं प्रजायते ।","यो मनःसुस्थिरो भावः सैवावस्था मनोन्मनी"],"iast":["mārute madhyasaṃcāre manaḥsthairyaṃ prajāyate |","yo manaḥsusthiro bhāvaḥ saivāvasthā manonmanī"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 11","title":"","sa":["पूरकान्ते तु कर्तव्यो बन्धो जालन्धराभिधः ।","कुम्भकान्ते रेचकादौ कर्तव्यस्तूड्डियाणकः"],"iast":["pūrakānte tu kartavyo bandho jālandharābhidhaḥ |","kumbhakānte recakādau kartavyastūḍḍiyāṇakaḥ"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 12","title":"","sa":["अधस्तात्कुञ्चनेमाशु कण्ठसङ्कोचने कृते ।","मध्ये पश्चिमतानेन स्यात्प्राणो ब्रह्मनाडिगः"],"iast":["adhastātkuñcanemāśu kaṇṭhasaṅkocane kṛte |","madhye paścimatānena syātprāṇo brahmanāḍigaḥ"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 13","title":"","sa":["अपानमूर्ध्वमुत्थाप्य प्राणं कण्ठादधो नयन् ।","योगी जराविनिर्मुक्तः षोडशो वयसा भवेत्"],"iast":["apānamūrdhvamutthāpya prāṇaṃ kaṇṭhādadho nayan |","yogī jarāvinirmuktaḥ ṣoḍaśo vayasā bhavet"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 14","title":"","sa":["सुखासनस्थो दक्षनाड्या बहिस्थं पवनं समाकृष्याकेशमानखाग्रं कुम्भयित्वा सव्यनाड्या रेचयेत् । तेन कपालशोधनं वातनाडीगतसर्वरोगसर्वविनाशनं भवति । हृदयादिकण्ठपर्यन्तं सस्वनं नासाभ्यां शनैः पवनमाकृष्य यथाशक्ति कुम्भयित्वा इडया विरेच्य गच्छंस्तिष्ठन्कुर्यात् । तेन श्लेष्महरं जठराग्निवर्धनं भवति । वक्त्रेण सीत्कारपूर्वकं वायुं गृहीत्वा यथाशक्ति कुम्भयित्वा नासाभ्यां रेचयेत् । तेन क्षुत्तृष्णालस्यनिद्रा न जायते । जिह्वया वायुं गृहीत्वा यथाशक्ति कुम्भयित्वा नासाभ्यां रेचयेत् । तेन गुल्मप्लीहज्वरपित्तक्षुधादीनि नश्यन्ति ॥ अथ कुम्भकः । स द्विविधः सहितः केवलश्चेति । रेचकपूरकयुक्तः सहितः तद्विवर्जितः केवलः । केवलसिद्धिपर्यन्तं सहितमभ्यसेत् । केवलकुम्भके सिद्धे त्रिषु लोकेषु न तस्य दुर्लभं भवति । केवलकुम्भकात्कुण्डलिनीबोधो जायते । ततः कृशवपुः प्रसन्नवदनो निर्मललोचनोऽभिव्यक्तनादो निर्मुक्तरोगजालो जितबिन्दुः पट्वग्निर्भवति । अन्तर्लक्ष्यं बहिर्दृष्टिर्निमेषोन्मेषवर्जिता । एषा सा वैष्णवी मुद्रा सर्वतन्त्रेषु गोपिता"],"iast":["sukhāsanastho dakṣanāḍyā bahisthaṃ pavanaṃ samākṛṣyākeśamānakhāgraṃ kumbhayitvā savyanāḍyā recayet |","tena kapālaśodhanaṃ vātanāḍīgatasarvarogasarvavināśanaṃ bhavati |","hṛdayādikaṇṭhaparyantaṃ sasvanaṃ nāsābhyāṃ śanaiḥ pavanamākṛṣya yathāśakti kumbhayitvā iḍayā virecya gacchaṃstiṣṭhankuryāt |","tena śleṣmaharaṃ jaṭharāgnivardhanaṃ bhavati |","vaktreṇa sītkārapūrvakaṃ vāyuṃ gṛhītvā yathāśakti kumbhayitvā nāsābhyāṃ recayet |","tena kṣuttṛṣṇālasyanidrā na jāyate |","jihvayā vāyuṃ gṛhītvā yathāśakti kumbhayitvā nāsābhyāṃ recayet |","tena gulmaplīhajvarapittakṣudhādīni naśyanti | atha kumbhakaḥ |","sa dvividhaḥ sahitaḥ kevalaśceti |","recakapūrakayuktaḥ sahitaḥ tadvivarjitaḥ kevalaḥ |","kevalasiddhiparyantaṃ sahitamabhyaset |","kevalakumbhake siddhe triṣu lokeṣu na tasya durlabhaṃ bhavati |","kevalakumbhakātkuṇḍalinībodho jāyate |","tataḥ kṛśavapuḥ prasannavadano nirmalalocano'bhivyaktanādo nirmuktarogajālo jitabinduḥ paṭvagnirbhavati |","antarlakṣyaṃ bahirdṛṣṭirnimeṣonmeṣavarjitā |","eṣā sā vaiṣṇavī mudrā sarvatantreṣu gopitā"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 15","title":"","sa":["अन्तर्लक्ष्यविलीनचित्तपवनो योगी सदा वर्तते","दृष्ट्या निश्चलतारया बहिरधः पश्यन्नपश्यन्नपि ।","मुद्रेयं खलु खेचरी भवति सा लक्ष्यैकताना शिवा","शून्याशून्यविवर्जितं स्फुरति सा तत्त्वं पदं वैष्णवी"],"iast":["antarlakṣyavilīnacittapavano yogī sadā vartate","dṛṣṭyā niścalatārayā bahiradhaḥ paśyannapaśyannapi |","mudreyaṃ khalu khecarī bhavati sā lakṣyaikatānā śivā","śūnyāśūnyavivarjitaṃ sphurati sā tattvaṃ padaṃ vaiṣṇavī"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 16","title":"","sa":["अर्धोन्मीलितलोचनः स्थिरमना नासाग्रदत्तेक्षणश्चन्द्रार्कावपि","लीनतामुपनयन्निष्पन्दभावोत्तरम् ।","ज्योतीरूपमशीषबाह्यरहितं देदीप्यमानं परं","तत्त्वं तत्परमस्ति वस्तुविषयं शाण्डिल्य विद्धीह तत्"],"iast":["ardhonmīlitalocanaḥ sthiramanā nāsāgradattekṣaṇaścandrārkāvapi","līnatāmupanayanniṣpandabhāvottaram |","jyotīrūpamaśīṣabāhyarahitaṃ dedīpyamānaṃ paraṃ","tattvaṃ tatparamasti vastuviṣayaṃ śāṇḍilya viddhīha tat"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 17","title":"","sa":["तारं ज्योतिषि संयोज्य किञ्चिदुन्नमयन्भ्रुवौ ।","पूर्वाभ्यासस्य मार्गोऽयमुन्मनीकारकः क्षणात्"],"iast":["tāraṃ jyotiṣi saṃyojya kiñcidunnamayanbhruvau |","pūrvābhyāsasya mārgo'yamunmanīkārakaḥ kṣaṇāt"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 18","title":"","sa":["तस्मात्खेचरीमुद्रामभ्यसेत् । तत उन्मनी भवति ।","ततो योगनिद्रा भवति । लब्धयोगनिद्रस्य योगिनः कालो नास्ति ।","शक्तिमध्ये मनः कृत्वा शक्तिं मानसमध्यगाम् ।","मनसा मन आलोक्य शाण्डिल्य त्वं सुखी भव"],"iast":["tasmātkhecarīmudrāmabhyaset |","tata unmanī bhavati |","tato yoganidrā bhavati |","labdhayoganidrasya yoginaḥ kālo nāsti |","śaktimadhye manaḥ kṛtvā śaktiṃ mānasamadhyagām |","manasā mana ālokya śāṇḍilya tvaṃ sukhī bhava"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 19","title":"","sa":["खमध्ये कुरु चात्मानमात्ममध्ये च खं कुरु ।","सर्वं च खमयं कृत्वा न किञ्चिदपि चिन्तय"],"iast":["khamadhye kuru cātmānamātmamadhye ca khaṃ kuru |","sarvaṃ ca khamayaṃ kṛtvā na kiñcidapi cintaya"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 20","title":"","sa":["बाह्यचिन्ता न कर्तव्या तथैवान्तरचिन्तिका ।","सर्वचिन्तां परित्यज्य चिन्मात्रपरमो भव"],"iast":["bāhyacintā na kartavyā tathaivāntaracintikā |","sarvacintāṃ parityajya cinmātraparamo bhava"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 21","title":"","sa":["कर्पूरमनले यद्वत्सैन्धवं सलिले यथा ।","तथा च लीयमानं च मनस्तत्त्वे विलीयते"],"iast":["karpūramanale yadvatsaindhavaṃ salile yathā |","tathā ca līyamānaṃ ca manastattve vilīyate"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 22","title":"","sa":["ज्ञेयं सर्वप्रतीतं च तज्ज्ञानं मन उच्यते ।","ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं समं नष्टं नान्यः पन्था द्वितीयकः"],"iast":["jñeyaṃ sarvapratītaṃ ca tajjñānaṃ mana ucyate |","jñānaṃ jñeyaṃ samaṃ naṣṭaṃ nānyaḥ panthā dvitīyakaḥ"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 23","title":"","sa":["ज्ञेयवस्तुपरित्यागाद्विलयं याति मानसम् ।","मानसे विलयं याते कैवल्यमवशिष्यते"],"iast":["jñeyavastuparityāgādvilayaṃ yāti mānasam |","mānase vilayaṃ yāte kaivalyamavaśiṣyate"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 24","title":"","sa":["द्वौ क्रमौ चित्तनाशस्य योगो ज्ञानं मुनीश्वर ।","योगस्तद्वृत्तिरोधो हि ज्ञानं सम्यगवेक्षणम्"],"iast":["dvau kramau cittanāśasya yogo jñānaṃ munīśvara |","yogastadvṛttirodho hi jñānaṃ samyagavekṣaṇam"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 25","title":"","sa":["तस्मिन्निरोधिते नूनमुपशान्तं मनो भवेत् ।","मनःस्पन्दोपशान्तायं संसारः प्रविलीयते"],"iast":["tasminnirodhite nūnamupaśāntaṃ mano bhavet |","manaḥspandopaśāntāyaṃ saṃsāraḥ pravilīyate"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 26","title":"","sa":["सूर्यालोकपरिस्पन्दशान्तौ व्यवहृतिर्यथा ।","शास्त्रसज्जनसम्पर्कवैराग्याभ्यासयोगतः"],"iast":["sūryālokaparispandaśāntau vyavahṛtiryathā |","śāstrasajjanasamparkavairāgyābhyāsayogataḥ"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 27","title":"","sa":["अनास्थायां कृतास्थायां पूर्वं संसारवृत्तिषु ।","यथाभिवाञ्छितध्यानाच्चिरमेकतयोहितात्"],"iast":["anāsthāyāṃ kṛtāsthāyāṃ pūrvaṃ saṃsāravṛttiṣu |","yathābhivāñchitadhyānācciramekatayohitāt"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 28","title":"","sa":["एकतत्त्वदृढाभ्यासात्प्राणस्पन्दो निरुध्यते ।","पूरकाद्यनिलायामादृढाभ्यासदखेदजात्"],"iast":["ekatattvadṛḍhābhyāsātprāṇaspando nirudhyate |","pūrakādyanilāyāmādṛḍhābhyāsadakhedajāt"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 29","title":"","sa":["एकान्तध्यानयोगाच्च मनःस्पन्दो निरुध्यते ।","ओङ्कारोच्चारणप्रान्तशब्दतत्त्वानुभावनात् ।","सुषुप्ते संविदा ज्ञाते प्राणस्पन्दो निरुध्यते"],"iast":["ekāntadhyānayogācca manaḥspando nirudhyate |","oṅkāroccāraṇaprāntaśabdatattvānubhāvanāt |","suṣupte saṃvidā jñāte prāṇaspando nirudhyate"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 30","title":"","sa":["तालुमूलगतां यत्नाज्जिह्वयाक्रम्य घण्टिकाम् ।","ऊर्ध्वरन्ध्रं गते प्राणे प्राणस्पन्दो निरुध्यते"],"iast":["tālumūlagatāṃ yatnājjihvayākramya ghaṇṭikām |","ūrdhvarandhraṃ gate prāṇe prāṇaspando nirudhyate"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 31","title":"","sa":["प्राणे गलितसंवित्तौ तालूर्ध्वं द्वादशान्तगे ।","अभ्यासादूर्ध्वरन्ध्रेण प्राणस्पन्दो निरुध्यते"],"iast":["prāṇe galitasaṃvittau tālūrdhvaṃ dvādaśāntage |","abhyāsādūrdhvarandhreṇa prāṇaspando nirudhyate"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 32","title":"","sa":["द्वादशाङ्गुलपर्यन्ते नासाग्रे विमलेऽम्बरे ।","संविद्दृशि प्रशाम्यन्त्यां प्राणस्पन्दो निरुध्यते"],"iast":["dvādaśāṅgulaparyante nāsāgre vimale'mbare |","saṃviddṛśi praśāmyantyāṃ prāṇaspando nirudhyate"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 33","title":"","sa":["भ्रूमध्ये तारकालोकशान्तावन्तमुपागते ।","चेतनैकतने बद्धे प्राणस्पन्दो निरुध्यते"],"iast":["bhrūmadhye tārakālokaśāntāvantamupāgate |"],"words":[],"lit":"cetanaikatane baddhe prāṇaspando nirudhyate","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 34","title":"","sa":["ओमित्येव यदुद्भूतं ज्ञानं ज्ञेयात्मकं शिवम् ।","असंस्पृष्टविकल्पांशं प्राणस्पन्दो निरुध्यते"],"iast":["omityeva yadudbhūtaṃ jñānaṃ jñeyātmakaṃ śivam |","asaṃspṛṣṭavikalpāṃśaṃ prāṇaspando nirudhyate"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 35","title":"","sa":["चिरकालं हृदेकान्तव्योमसंवेदनान्मुने ।","अवासनमनोध्यानात्प्राणस्पन्दो निरुध्यते"],"iast":["cirakālaṃ hṛdekāntavyomasaṃvedanānmune |","avāsanamanodhyānātprāṇaspando nirudhyate"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 36","title":"","sa":["एभिः क्रमैस्तथान्यैश्च नानासंकल्पकल्पितैः ।","नानादेशिकवक्त्रस्थैः प्राणस्पन्दो निरुध्यते"],"iast":["ebhiḥ kramaistathānyaiśca nānāsaṃkalpakalpitaiḥ |","nānādeśikavaktrasthaiḥ prāṇaspando nirudhyate"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 37","title":"","sa":["आकुञ्चनेन कुण्डलिन्याः कवाटमुद्घाट्य मोक्षद्वारं विभेदयेत् । येन मार्गेण गन्तव्यं तद्द्वारं मुखेनाच्छाद्य प्रसुप्ता कुण्डलिनी कुटिलाकारा सर्पवद्वेष्टिता भवति । सा शक्तिर्येन चालिता स्यात्स तु मुक्तो भवति । सा कुण्डलिनी कण्ठोर्ध्वभागे सुप्ता चेद्योगिनां मुक्तये भवति । बन्धनायाधो मूढानाम् । इडादिमार्गद्वयं विहाय सुषुम्नामार्गेणागच्छेत्तद्विष्णोः परमं पदम् । मरुदभ्यसनं सर्वं मनोयुक्तं समभ्यसेत्।ह् इतरत्र न कर्तव्या मनोवृत्तिर्मनीषिणा"],"iast":["ākuñcanena kuṇḍalinyāḥ kavāṭamudghāṭya mokṣadvāraṃ vibhedayet |","yena mārgeṇa gantavyaṃ taddvāraṃ mukhenācchādya prasuptā kuṇḍalinī kuṭilākārā sarpavadveṣṭitā bhavati |","sā śaktiryena cālitā syātsa tu mukto bhavati |","sā kuṇḍalinī kaṇṭhordhvabhāge suptā cedyogināṃ muktaye bhavati |","bandhanāyādho mūḍhānām |","iḍādimārgadvayaṃ vihāya suṣumnāmārgeṇāgacchettadviṣṇoḥ paramaṃ padam |","marudabhyasanaṃ sarvaṃ manoyuktaṃ samabhyaset|h itaratra na kartavyā manovṛttirmanīṣiṇā"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 38","title":"","sa":["दिवा न पूजयेद्विष्णुं रात्रौ नैव प्रपूजयेत् ।","सततं पूजयेद्विष्णुं दिवारात्रं न पूजयेत्"],"iast":["divā na pūjayedviṣṇuṃ rātrau naiva prapūjayet |","satataṃ pūjayedviṣṇuṃ divārātraṃ na pūjayet"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 39","title":"","sa":["सुषिरो ज्ञानजनकः पञ्चस्रोतःसमन्वितः ।","तिष्ठते खेचरी मुद्रा तस्मिन्स्थाने न संशयः"],"iast":["suṣiro jñānajanakaḥ pañcasrotaḥsamanvitaḥ |","tiṣṭhate khecarī mudrā tasminsthāne na saṃśayaḥ"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 40","title":"","sa":["सव्यदक्षिणनाडीस्थो मध्ये चरति मारुतः ।","तिष्ठतः खेचरी मुद्रा तस्मिन्स्थाने न संशयः"],"iast":["savyadakṣiṇanāḍīstho madhye carati mārutaḥ |","tiṣṭhataḥ khecarī mudrā tasminsthāne na saṃśayaḥ"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 41","title":"","sa":["इडापिङ्गलयोर्मध्ये शून्यं चैवानिलं ग्रसेत् ।","तिष्ठन्ती खेचरी मुद्रा तत्र सत्यं प्रतिष्ठितम्"],"iast":["iḍāpiṅgalayormadhye śūnyaṃ caivānilaṃ graset |","tiṣṭhantī khecarī mudrā tatra satyaṃ pratiṣṭhitam"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 42","title":"","sa":["सोमसूर्यद्वयोर्मध्ये निरालम्बतले पुनः ।","संस्थिता व्योमचक्रे सा मुद्रा नाम्ना च खेचरी"],"iast":["somasūryadvayormadhye nirālambatale punaḥ |","saṃsthitā vyomacakre sā mudrā nāmnā ca khecarī"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 43","title":"","sa":["छेदनचालनदाहैः फलां परां जिह्वां कृत्वा दृष्टिं भ्रूमध्ये स्थाप्य कपालकुहरे जिह्वा विपरीतगा यदा भवति तदा खेचरी मुद्रा जायते । जिह्वा चित्तं च खे चरति तेनोर्ध्वजिह्वः पुमानमृतो भवति । वामपादमूलेन योनिं सम्पीड्य दक्षिणपादं प्रसार्य तं कराभ्यां धृत्वा नासाभ्यां वायुमापूर्य कण्ठबन्धं समारोप्योर्ध्वतो वायुं धारयेत् । तेन सर्वक्लेशहानिः । ततः पीयूषमिव विषं जीर्यते । क्षयगुल्मगुदावर्तजीर्णत्वगादिदोषा नश्यन्ति । एष प्राणजयोपायः सर्वमृत्यूपघातकः । वामपादपार्ष्णिं योनिस्थाने नियोज्य दक्षिणचरणं वामोरूपरि संस्थाप्य वायुमापूर्य हृदये चुबुकं निधाय योनिमाकुञ्च्य  मनोमध्ये यथाशक्ति धारयित्वा स्वात्मानं भावयेत् । तेनापरोक्षसिद्धिः ।","बाह्यात्प्राणं समाकृष्य पूरयित्वोदरे स्थितम् ।","नाभिमध्ये च नासाग्रे पदाङ्गुष्ठे च यत्नतः"],"iast":["chedanacālanadāhaiḥ phalāṃ parāṃ jihvāṃ kṛtvā dṛṣṭiṃ bhrūmadhye sthāpya kapālakuhare jihvā viparītagā yadā bhavati tadā khecarī mudrā jāyate |","jihvā cittaṃ ca khe carati tenordhvajihvaḥ pumānamṛto bhavati |","vāmapādamūlena yoniṃ sampīḍya dakṣiṇapādaṃ prasārya taṃ karābhyāṃ dhṛtvā nāsābhyāṃ vāyumāpūrya kaṇṭhabandhaṃ samāropyordhvato vāyuṃ dhārayet |","tena sarvakleśahāniḥ |","tataḥ pīyūṣamiva viṣaṃ jīryate |","kṣayagulmagudāvartajīrṇatvagādidoṣā naśyanti |","eṣa prāṇajayopāyaḥ sarvamṛtyūpaghātakaḥ |","vāmapādapārṣṇiṃ yonisthāne niyojya dakṣiṇacaraṇaṃ vāmorūpari saṃsthāpya vāyumāpūrya hṛdaye cubukaṃ nidhāya yonimākuñcya  manomadhye yathāśakti dhārayitvā svātmānaṃ bhāvayet |","tenāparokṣasiddhiḥ |","bāhyātprāṇaṃ samākṛṣya pūrayitvodare sthitam |","nābhimadhye ca nāsāgre padāṅguṣṭhe ca yatnataḥ"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 44","title":"","sa":["धारयेन्मनसा प्राणं सन्ध्याकालेषु वा सदा ।","सर्वरोगविनिर्मुक्तो भवेद्योगी गतक्लमः"],"iast":["dhārayenmanasā prāṇaṃ sandhyākāleṣu vā sadā |","sarvarogavinirmukto bhavedyogī gataklamaḥ"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 45","title":"","sa":["नासाग्रे वायुविजयं भवति । नाभिमध्ये सर्वरोगविनाशः ।","पादाङ्गुष्ठदारणाच्छरीरलघुता भवति ।","रसनाद्वायुमाकृष्य यः पिबेत्सतततं नरः ।","श्रमदाहौ तु न स्यातां नश्यन्ति व्याधयस्तथा"],"iast":["nāsāgre vāyuvijayaṃ bhavati |","nābhimadhye sarvarogavināśaḥ |","pādāṅguṣṭhadāraṇāccharīralaghutā bhavati |","rasanādvāyumākṛṣya yaḥ pibetsatatataṃ naraḥ |","śramadāhau tu na syātāṃ naśyanti vyādhayastathā"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 46","title":"","sa":["सन्ध्ययोर्ब्राह्मणः काले वायुमाकृष्य यः पिबेत् ।","त्रिमासात्तस्य कल्याणी जायते वाक् सरस्वती"],"iast":["sandhyayorbrāhmaṇaḥ kāle vāyumākṛṣya yaḥ pibet |","trimāsāttasya kalyāṇī jāyate vāk sarasvatī"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 47","title":"","sa":["एवं षण्मासाभ्यासात्सर्वरोगनिवृत्तिः ।","जिह्वया वायुमानीय जिह्वामूले निरोधयेत् ।","यः पिबेदमृतं विद्वान्सकलं भद्रमश्नुते"],"iast":["evaṃ ṣaṇmāsābhyāsātsarvaroganivṛttiḥ |","jihvayā vāyumānīya jihvāmūle nirodhayet |","yaḥ pibedamṛtaṃ vidvānsakalaṃ bhadramaśnute"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 48","title":"","sa":["आत्मन्यात्मानमिडया धारयित्वा भ्रुवोन्तरे ।","विभेद्य त्रिदशाहारं व्याधिस्थोऽपि विमुच्यते"],"iast":["ātmanyātmānamiḍayā dhārayitvā bhruvontare |","vibhedya tridaśāhāraṃ vyādhistho'pi vimucyate"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 49","title":"","sa":["नाडीभ्यां वायुमारोप्य नाभौ तुन्दस्य पार्श्वयोः ।","घटिकैकां वहेद्यस्तु व्याधिभिः स विमुच्यते"],"iast":["nāḍībhyāṃ vāyumāropya nābhau tundasya pārśvayoḥ |","ghaṭikaikāṃ vahedyastu vyādhibhiḥ sa vimucyate"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 50","title":"","sa":["मासमेकं त्रिसन्ध्यं तु जिह्वयारोप्य मारुतम् ।","विभेद्य त्रिदशाहारं धारयेत्तुन्दमध्यमे"],"iast":["māsamekaṃ trisandhyaṃ tu jihvayāropya mārutam |","vibhedya tridaśāhāraṃ dhārayettundamadhyame"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§7 · 51","title":"","sa":["ज्वराः सर्वेऽपि नश्यन्ति विषाणि विविधानि च ।","मुहूर्तमपि यो नित्यं नासाग्रे मनसा सह","सर्वं तरति पाप्मानं तस्य जन्म शतार्जितम् ।","तारसंयमात्सकलविषयज्ञानं भवति ।","नासाग्रे चित्तसंयमादिन्द्रलोकज्ञानम् ।","तदधश्चित्तसंयमादग्निलोकज्ञानम् ।","चक्षुषि चित्तसंयमात्सर्वलोकज्ञानम् ।","श्रोत्रे चित्तस्य संयमाद्यमलोकज्ञानम् ।","तत्पार्श्वे संयमान्निरृतिलोकज्ञानम् ।","पृष्ठभागे संयमाद्वरुणलोकज्ञानम् ।","वामकर्णे संयमाद्वायुलोकज्ञानम् ।","कण्ठे संयमात्सोमलोकज्ञानम् ।","वामचक्षुषि संयमाच्छिवलोकज्ञानम् ।","मूर्ध्नि संयमाद्ब्रह्मलोकज्ञानम् ।","पादादोभागे संयमादतललोकज्ञानम् ।","पादे संयमाद्वितललोकज्ञानम् ।","पादसन्धौ संयमान्नितललोकज्ञानम् ।","जङ्घे संयमात्सुतललोकज्ञानम् ।","जानौ संयमान्महातललोकज्ञानम् ।","ऊरौ चित्तसंयमाद्रसातललोकज्ञानम् ।","कटौ चित्तसंयमात्तलातललोकज्ञानम् ।","नाभौ चित्तसंयमाद्भूलोकज्ञानम् ।","कुक्षौ संयमाद्भुवर्लोकज्ञानम् ।","हृदि चित्तस्य संयमात्स्वर्लोकज्ञानम् ।","हृदयोर्ध्वभागे चित्तसंयमान्महर्लोकज्ञानम् ।","कण्ठे चित्तसंयमाज्जनोलोकज्ञानम् ।","भ्रूमध्ये चित्तसंयमात्तपोलोकज्ञानम् ।","मूर्ध्नि चित्तसंयमात्सत्यलोकज्ञानम् ।","धर्माधर्मसंयमादतीतानागतज्ञानम् ।","तत्तज्जन्तुध्वनौ चित्तसंयमात्सर्वजन्तुरुतज्ञानम् ।","संचितकर्मणि चित्तसंयमात्पूर्वजातिज्ञानम् ।","परचित्ते चित्तसंयमात्परचित्तज्ञानम् ।","कायरूपे चित्तसंयमादन्यादृश्यरूपम् ।","बले चित्तसंयमाद्धनुमदादिबलम् ।","सूर्ये चित्तसंयमाद्भुवनज्ञानम् ।","चन्द्रे चित्तसंयमात्ताराव्यूहज्ञानम् ।","ध्रुवे तद्गतिदर्शनम् । स्वार्थसंयमात्पुरुषज्ञानम् ।","नाभिचक्रे कायव्यूहज्ञानम् । कण्ठकूपे क्षुत्पिपासा निवृत्तिः ।","कूर्मनाड्यां स्थैर्यम् । तारे सिद्धदर्शनम् ।","कायाकाशसंयमादाकाशगमनम् ।","तत्तत्स्थाने संयमात्तत्तत्सिद्धयो भवन्ति"],"iast":["jvarāḥ sarve'pi naśyanti viṣāṇi vividhāni ca |","muhūrtamapi yo nityaṃ nāsāgre manasā saha","sarvaṃ tarati pāpmānaṃ tasya janma śatārjitam |","tārasaṃyamātsakalaviṣayajñānaṃ bhavati |","nāsāgre cittasaṃyamādindralokajñānam |","tadadhaścittasaṃyamādagnilokajñānam |","cakṣuṣi cittasaṃyamātsarvalokajñānam |","śrotre cittasya saṃyamādyamalokajñānam |","tatpārśve saṃyamānnirṛtilokajñānam |","pṛṣṭhabhāge saṃyamādvaruṇalokajñānam |","vāmakarṇe saṃyamādvāyulokajñānam |","kaṇṭhe saṃyamātsomalokajñānam |","vāmacakṣuṣi saṃyamācchivalokajñānam |","mūrdhni saṃyamādbrahmalokajñānam |","pādādobhāge saṃyamādatalalokajñānam |","pāde saṃyamādvitalalokajñānam |","pādasandhau saṃyamānnitalalokajñānam |","jaṅghe saṃyamātsutalalokajñānam |","jānau saṃyamānmahātalalokajñānam |","ūrau cittasaṃyamādrasātalalokajñānam |","kaṭau cittasaṃyamāttalātalalokajñānam |","nābhau cittasaṃyamādbhūlokajñānam |","kukṣau saṃyamādbhuvarlokajñānam |","hṛdi cittasya saṃyamātsvarlokajñānam |","hṛdayordhvabhāge cittasaṃyamānmaharlokajñānam |","kaṇṭhe cittasaṃyamājjanolokajñānam |","bhrūmadhye cittasaṃyamāttapolokajñānam |","mūrdhni cittasaṃyamātsatyalokajñānam |","dharmādharmasaṃyamādatītānāgatajñānam |","tattajjantudhvanau cittasaṃyamātsarvajanturutajñānam |","saṃcitakarmaṇi cittasaṃyamātpūrvajātijñānam |","paracitte cittasaṃyamātparacittajñānam |","kāyarūpe cittasaṃyamādanyādṛśyarūpam |","bale cittasaṃyamāddhanumadādibalam |","sūrye cittasaṃyamādbhuvanajñānam |","candre cittasaṃyamāttārāvyūhajñānam |","dhruve tadgatidarśanam | svārthasaṃyamātpuruṣajñānam |","nābhicakre kāyavyūhajñānam | kaṇṭhakūpe kṣutpipāsā nivṛttiḥ |","kūrmanāḍyāṃ sthairyam | tāre siddhadarśanam |","kāyākāśasaṃyamādākāśagamanam |","tattatsthāne saṃyamāttattatsiddhayo bhavanti"],"words":[],"lit":"Closing prose of §7 (saṃyama-sites):","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["[Then a long discourse on saṃyama at various body-points and the resulting knowledge:]<br><br>By saṃyama on the tip of the nose comes knowledge of all sense-objects. By saṃyama on the eye comes knowledge of all worlds. By saṃyama on the ear comes knowledge of Yama-loka. By saṃyama on its side, knowledge of Nirṛti-loka. On the back, knowledge of Varuṇa-loka. On the left ear, knowledge of Vāyu-loka. On the throat, knowledge of Soma-loka. On the left eye, knowledge of Śiva-loka. On the crown, knowledge of Brahma-loka. On the lower portion of the feet, knowledge of Atala-loka. On the foot, of Vitala. On the foot-joint, of Nitala. On the shank, of Sutala. On the knee, of Mahātala. On the thigh, of Rasātala. On the hip, of Talātala. On the navel, of Bhū-loka. On the abdomen, of Bhuvar-loka. On the heart, of Svar-loka. On the upper-heart, of Mahar-loka. On the throat, of Jana-loka. Between the brows, of Tapo-loka. On the crown, of Satya-loka.<br><br>By saṃyama on dharma and adharma — knowledge of past and future. On the sound of various beings — knowledge of the speech of all creatures. On accumulated karma — knowledge of past lives. On another's mind — knowledge of others' minds. On the body-form — invisibility. On strength — strength like Hanumān etc. On the sun — knowledge of worlds. On the moon — knowledge of constellations. On Dhruva — knowledge of their motions. By saṃyama on the navel-cakra — knowledge of body-structure. On the throat-pit — cessation of hunger and thirst. On the kūrma-nāḍī — stability. On the cranial light — vision of the perfected ones. On body-space (kāyākāśa) — movement through space.<br><br>The corresponding siddhis arise according to where saṃyama is fixed."]}]},{"t":"","u":[{"ref":"§8","title":"Pratyāhāra (Five-Fold)","sa":["अथ प्रत्याहारः । स पञ्चविधः विषयेषु विचरतामिन्द्रियाणां बलादाहरणं प्रत्याहरः । यद्यत्पश्यति तत्सर्वमामेति प्रत्याहारः । नित्यविहितकर्मफलत्यागः प्रत्याहारः । सर्वविषयपराङ्मुखत्वं प्रत्याहारः । अष्टादशसु मर्मस्थानेषु क्रमाद्धारणं प्रत्याहारः । पादाङ्गुष्ठगुल्फजङ्घाजानूरुपायुमेढ्रनाभिहृदयकण्ठकूपतालुनासाक्षिभ्रूमध्यललाटमूर्ध्नि स्थानानि । तेषु क्रमादारोहावरोहक्रमेण प्रत्याहरेत्"],"iast":["atha pratyāhāraḥ | sa pañcavidhaḥ viṣayeṣu vicaratāmindriyāṇāṃ balādāharaṇaṃ pratyāharaḥ | yadyatpaśyati tatsarvamāmeti pratyāhāraḥ | nityavihitakarmaphalatyāgaḥ pratyāhāraḥ | sarvaviṣayaparāṅmukhatvaṃ pratyāhāraḥ | aṣṭādaśasu marmasthāneṣu kramāddhāraṇaṃ pratyāhāraḥ | pādāṅguṣṭhagulphajaṅghājānūrupāyumeḍhranābhihṛdayakaṇṭhakūpatālunāsākṣibhrūmadhyalalāṭamūrdhni sthānāni | teṣu kramādārohāvarohakrameṇa pratyāharet"],"words":[],"lit":"Pratyāhāra is five-fold: (1) The forcible withdrawal of the senses wandering among sense-objects. (2) Seeing everything one sees as the Self. (3) The renunciation of the fruits of one's daily-prescribed actions. (4) Turning away from all sense-objects. (5) Sequential holding (dhāraṇā) at the eighteen vital points (marma-sthāna).<br><br>These vital points are: the two big toes, ankles, calves, knees, thighs, anus, genitals, navel, heart, throat-pit, palate, nose, eyes, between the brows, forehead, and crown — sequentially in ascending and descending order. Thus one performs pratyāhāra.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§9","title":"Dhāraṇā (Threefold)","sa":["अथ धारणा । सा त्रिविधा । आत्मनि मनोधारणं दहराकाशे बाह्याकाशधारणं पृथिव्यप्तेजोवाय्वाकाशेषु पञ्चमूर्तिधारणं चेति"],"iast":["atha dhāraṇā | sā trividhā | ātmani manodhāraṇaṃ daharākāśe bāhyākāśadhāraṇaṃ pṛthivyaptejovāyvākāśeṣu pañcamūrtidhāraṇaṃ ceti"],"words":[],"lit":"Dhāraṇā is threefold: holding the mind in the Self; holding it in the inner ether (dahara-ākāśa); holding it in the outer ether (bāhya-ākāśa); and the five-fold elemental dhāraṇā in earth, water, fire, air, and space.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§10","title":"Dhyāna (Saguṇa and Nirguṇa)","sa":["अथ ध्यानम् । तद्द्विविधं सगुणं निर्गुणं चेति ।","सगुणं मूर्तिध्यानम् । निर्गुणमात्मयाथात्म्यम्"],"iast":["atha dhyānam | taddvividhaṃ saguṇaṃ nirguṇaṃ ceti |","saguṇaṃ mūrtidhyānam | nirguṇamātmayāthātmyam"],"words":[],"lit":"Dhyāna is twofold: with qualities (saguṇa) and without qualities (nirguṇa). Saguṇa-dhyāna is meditation on a form. Nirguṇa-dhyāna is meditation on the Self as it is.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§11","title":"Samādhi","sa":["अथ समाधिः । जीवात्मपरमात्मैक्यावस्थात्रिपुटीरहिता","परमानन्दस्वरूपा शुद्धचैतन्यात्मिका भवति","इति प्रथमोऽध्यायः ॥ १ ॥"],"iast":["atha samādhiḥ | jīvātmaparamātmaikyāvasthātripuṭīrahitā","paramānandasvarūpā śuddhacaitanyātmikā bhavati","iti prathamo 'dhyāyaḥ || 1 ||  —  \"Thus the First Chapter.\""],"words":[],"lit":"Samādhi is the state of union of the individual self (jīvātma) and the supreme Self (paramātma), free from the triad (knower-known-knowing). It is the form of supreme bliss (paramānanda) and pure consciousness (śuddha-caitanya).","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"Adhyāya 2","title":"Brahma-Vidyā","sa":["अथ ह शाण्डिल्यो ह वै ब्रह्मऋषिश्चतुर्षु वेदेषु","ब्रह्मविद्यामलभमानः किं नामेत्यथर्वाणं","भगवन्तमुपसन्नः पप्रच्छाधीहि भगवन् ब्रह्मविद्यां","येन श्रेयोऽवाप्स्यामीति । स होवाचाथर्वा शाण्डिल्य सत्यं","विज्ञानमनन्तं ब्रह्म यस्मिन्निदमोतं च प्रोतं च ।","यस्मिन्निदं सं च विचैति सर्वं यस्मिन्विज्ञाते सर्वमिदं","विज्ञातं भवति । तदपाणिपादमचक्षुःश्रोत्रमजिह्वमशरीरमग्राह्यमनिर्देश्यम् । यतो वाचो निवर्तन्ते । अप्राप्य मनसा","सह । यत्केवलं ज्ञानगम्यम् । प्रज्ञा च यस्मात्प्रसृता","पुराणी । यदेकमद्वितीयम् । आकाशवत्सर्वगतं सुसूक्ष्मं","निरञ्जनं निष्क्रियं सन्मात्रं चिदानन्दैकरसं शिवं","प्रशान्तममृतं तत्परं च ब्रह्म । तत्त्वमसि । तज्ज्ञानेन हि","विजानीहि य एको देव आत्मशक्तिप्रधानः सर्वज्ञः सर्वेश्वरः","सर्वभूतान्तरात्मा सर्वभूताधिवासः सर्वभूतनिगूढो","भूतयोनिर्योगैकगम्यः । यश्च विश्वं सृजति विश्वं बिभर्ति","विश्वं भुङ्क्ते स आत्मा । आत्मनि तं तं लोकं विजानीहि । मा","शोचीरात्मविज्ञानी शोकस्यान्तं गमिष्यति ॥","इति द्वितीयोऽध्यायः","इति द्वितीयोऽध्यायः ॥ २ ॥"],"iast":["atha ha śāṇḍilyo ha vai brahmaṛṣiścaturṣu vedeṣu","brahmavidyāmalabhamānaḥ kiṃ nāmetyatharvāṇaṃ","bhagavantamupasannaḥ papracchādhīhi bhagavan brahmavidyāṃ","yena śreyo'vāpsyāmīti | sa hovācātharvā śāṇḍilya satyaṃ","vijñānamanantaṃ brahma yasminnidamotaṃ ca protaṃ ca |","yasminnidaṃ saṃ ca vicaiti sarvaṃ yasminvijñāte sarvamidaṃ","vijñātaṃ bhavati | tadapāṇipādamacakṣuḥśrotramajihvamaśarīramagrāhyamanirdeśyam | yato vāco nivartante | aprāpya manasā","saha | yatkevalaṃ jñānagamyam | prajñā ca yasmātprasṛtā","purāṇī | yadekamadvitīyam | ākāśavatsarvagataṃ susūkṣmaṃ","nirañjanaṃ niṣkriyaṃ sanmātraṃ cidānandaikarasaṃ śivaṃ","praśāntamamṛtaṃ tatparaṃ ca brahma | tattvamasi | tajjñānena hi","vijānīhi ya eko deva ātmaśaktipradhānaḥ sarvajñaḥ sarveśvaraḥ","sarvabhūtāntarātmā sarvabhūtādhivāsaḥ sarvabhūtanigūḍho","bhūtayoniryogaikagamyaḥ | yaśca viśvaṃ sṛjati viśvaṃ bibharti","viśvaṃ bhuṅkte sa ātmā | ātmani taṃ taṃ lokaṃ vijānīhi | mā","śocīrātmavijñānī śokasyāntaṃ gamiṣyati ||","iti dvitīyo'dhyāyaḥ","iti dvitīyo 'dhyāyaḥ || 2 ||  —  \"Thus the Second Chapter.\""],"words":[],"lit":"Then the brahmā-ṛṣi Śāṇḍilya, not having obtained brahma-vidyā in the four Vedas, approached the venerable Atharvan and asked: \"Teach me, O Lord, brahma-vidyā by which I may obtain the highest good.\"<br><br>Atharvan said: \"O Śāṇḍilya, Brahman is Truth, Knowledge, Infinite — in whom this whole [universe] is woven, in whom this entire [creation] dissolves; knowing whom, all this is known. That is without hands, without feet, without eyes, without ears, without tongue, without body — ungraspable, indescribable. From which words turn back, having not reached, together with mind. Which is to be known by pure knowledge alone. From which the ancient wisdom flows forth. That which is one, without a second; like space, all-pervading, very subtle, stainless, motionless, sat-mātra (pure being), of the one essence of consciousness-bliss, auspicious, calm, immortal — that supreme Brahman is what you are (tat tvam asi). Know it by knowledge.<br><br>He alone is the one God, predominant in self-power, all-knowing, lord of all, inner-Self of all beings, dweller in all beings, hidden in all beings, the source of beings, attainable only by yoga. He who creates, sustains, enjoys the universe — he is the Ātman. In the Ātman, know that world. Do not grieve. The knower of the Self goes beyond sorrow.\"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]}]},{"t":"Adhyāya 3 — The Three Forms of Brahman + Dattātreya Verses","u":[{"ref":"§1","title":"The Three Forms of Brahman","sa":["अथैनं शाण्डिल्योऽथर्वाणं पप्रच्छ यदेकमक्षरं","निष्क्रियं शिवं सन्मात्रं परंब्रह्म । तस्मात्कथमिदं","विश्वं जायते कथं स्थीयते कथमस्मिंल्लीयते । तन्मे संशयं","छेत्तुमर्हसीति । स होवाचाथर्वा सत्यं शाण्डिल्य परंब्रह्म","निष्क्रियमक्षरमिति । अथाप्यस्यारूपस्य ब्रह्मणस्त्रीणि","रूपाणि भवन्ति सकलं निष्कलं सकलनिष्कलं चेति ।","यत्सत्यं विज्ञानमानन्दं निष्क्रियं निरञ्जनं सर्वगतं","सुसूक्ष्मं सर्वतोमुखमनिर्देश्यममृतमस्ति तदिदं निष्कलं","रूपम् । अथास्य या सहजास्त्यविद्या मूलप्रकृतिर्माया","लोहितशुक्लकृष्णा । तया सहायवान् देवः कृष्णपिङ्गलो","ममेश्वर ईष्टे । तदिदमस्य सकलनिष्कलं रूपम् ॥ अथैष","ज्ञानमयेन तपसा चीयमानोऽकामयत बहु स्यां प्रजायेयेति ।","अथैतस्मात्तप्यमानात्सत्यकामात्त्रीण्यक्षराण्यजायन्त । तिस्रो","व्याहृतयस्त्रिपदा गायत्री त्रयो वेदास्त्रयो देवास्त्रयो वर्णास्त्रयोऽग्नयश्च","जायन्ते । योऽसौ देवो भगवान्सर्वैश्वर्यसम्पन्नः सर्वव्यापी","सर्वभूतानां हृदये संनिविष्टो मायावी मायया क्रीडति स ब्रह्मा","स विष्णुः स रुद्रः स इन्द्रः स सर्वे देवाः सर्वाणि भूतानि स एव","पुरस्तात्स एव पश्चात्स एवोत्तरतः स एव दक्षिणतः स एवाधस्तात्स","एवोपरिष्टात्स एव सर्वम् । अथास्य देवस्यात्मशक्तेरात्मक्रीडस्य","भक्तानुकंपिनो दत्तात्रेयरूपा सुरूपा तनूरवासा इन्दीवरदलप्रख्या","चतुर्बाहुरघोरापापकशिनी । तदिदमस्य सकलं रूपम्"],"iast":["athainaṃ śāṇḍilyo'tharvāṇaṃ papraccha yadekamakṣaraṃ","niṣkriyaṃ śivaṃ sanmātraṃ paraṃbrahma | tasmātkathamidaṃ","viśvaṃ jāyate kathaṃ sthīyate kathamasmiṃllīyate | tanme saṃśayaṃ","chettumarhasīti | sa hovācātharvā satyaṃ śāṇḍilya paraṃbrahma","niṣkriyamakṣaramiti | athāpyasyārūpasya brahmaṇastrīṇi","rūpāṇi bhavanti sakalaṃ niṣkalaṃ sakalaniṣkalaṃ ceti |","yatsatyaṃ vijñānamānandaṃ niṣkriyaṃ nirañjanaṃ sarvagataṃ","susūkṣmaṃ sarvatomukhamanirdeśyamamṛtamasti tadidaṃ niṣkalaṃ","rūpam | athāsya yā sahajāstyavidyā mūlaprakṛtirmāyā","lohitaśuklakṛṣṇā | tayā sahāyavān devaḥ kṛṣṇapiṅgalo","mameśvara īṣṭe | tadidamasya sakalaniṣkalaṃ rūpam || athaiṣa","jñānamayena tapasā cīyamāno'kāmayata bahu syāṃ prajāyeyeti |","athaitasmāttapyamānātsatyakāmāttrīṇyakṣarāṇyajāyanta | tisro","vyāhṛtayastripadā gāyatrī trayo vedāstrayo devāstrayo varṇāstrayo'gnayaśca","jāyante | yo'sau devo bhagavānsarvaiśvaryasampannaḥ sarvavyāpī","sarvabhūtānāṃ hṛdaye saṃniviṣṭo māyāvī māyayā krīḍati sa brahmā","sa viṣṇuḥ sa rudraḥ sa indraḥ sa sarve devāḥ sarvāṇi bhūtāni sa eva","purastātsa eva paścātsa evottarataḥ sa eva dakṣiṇataḥ sa evādhastātsa","evopariṣṭātsa eva sarvam | athāsya devasyātmaśakterātmakrīḍasya","bhaktānukaṃpino dattātreyarūpā surūpā tanūravāsā indīvaradalaprakhyā","caturbāhuraghorāpāpakaśinī | tadidamasya sakalaṃ rūpam"],"words":[],"lit":"Then Śāṇḍilya asked Atharvan: \"If the One imperishable, motionless, auspicious, pure being — the supreme Brahman — is so, how does this universe arise from it? How is it sustained? How does it dissolve into it? Resolve my doubt.\"<br><br>Atharvan said: \"Indeed, O Śāṇḍilya, the supreme Brahman is motionless, imperishable. Yet of this formless Brahman there arise three forms: with-parts (sakala), without-parts (niṣkala), and with-and-without-parts (sakala-niṣkala). That which is Truth, Knowledge, Bliss, motionless, stainless, all-pervading, very subtle, all-faced, indescribable, immortal — this is the niṣkala (partless) form.<br><br>Now, his innate ignorance — the root prakṛti, the māyā — is red, white, and black (tri-colored, the three guṇas). Together with her, the assisting deity, the dark-tawny (Kṛṣṇa-Piṅgala), my Lord rules. This is his sakala-niṣkala (mixed) form.<br><br>Then he, [being] grown by knowledge-form tapas, desired: 'May I be many; may I procreate.' From him, performing tapas, satisfied with truth-desires, three syllables were born: the three vyāhṛtis, the three-stepped Gāyatrī, the three Vedas, the three deities, the three colors, and the three fires. He, the Lord Bhagavān, possessing all powers, all-pervading, seated in the heart of all beings, sporting with māyā as a magician — he is Brahmā, he is Viṣṇu, he is Rudra, he is Indra, he is all the gods, all beings. He alone is in front, behind, on the north, on the south, below, above. He is everything.<br><br>Of that God's Self-power, sporting in his own play, compassionate to devotees — there is the four-armed Dattātreya form, beautiful in body, like the petals of a blue lotus, fierce against sin. This is his sakala (full) form.","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]}]},{"t":"§2 — Etymologies and the Dattātreya Verses","u":[{"ref":"§2","title":"Etymologies and the Dattātreya Verses","sa":["अथ हैनमथर्वाणं शाण्डिल्यः पप्रच्छ भगवन्सन्मात्रं","चिदानन्दैकरसं कस्मादुच्यते परं ब्रह्मेति । स होवाचाथर्वा","यस्माच्च बृहति बृंहयति च सर्वं तस्मादुच्यते परंब्रह्मेति ।","अथ कस्मादुच्यते आत्मेति । यस्मात्सर्वमाप्नोति सर्वमादत्ते सर्वमत्ति","च तस्मादुच्यते आत्मेति । अथ कस्मादुच्यते महेश्वर इति । यस्मान्महत","ईशः शब्दध्वन्या चात्मशक्त्या च महत ईशते तस्मादुच्यते","महेश्वर इति । अथ कस्मादुच्यते दत्तात्रेय इति । यस्मात्सुदुश्चरं","तपस्तप्यमानायात्रये पुत्रकामायातितरां तुष्टेन भगवता","ज्योतिर्मयेनात्मैव दत्तो यस्माच्चानसूयायामत्रेस्तनयोऽभवत्तस्मादुच्यते दत्तात्रेय इति । अथ योऽस्य निरुक्तानि वेद स सर्वं वेद ।","अथ यो ह वै विद्ययैनं परमुपास्ते सोऽहमिति स ब्रह्मविद्भवति ॥","अत्रैते श्लोका भवन्ति ॥","दत्तात्रेयं शिवं शान्तमिन्द्रनीलनिभं प्रभुम् ।","आत्ममायारतं देवमवधूतं दिगम्बरम्"],"iast":["atha hainamatharvāṇaṃ śāṇḍilyaḥ papraccha bhagavansanmātraṃ","cidānandaikarasaṃ kasmāducyate paraṃ brahmeti | sa hovācātharvā","yasmācca bṛhati bṛṃhayati ca sarvaṃ tasmāducyate paraṃbrahmeti |","atha kasmāducyate ātmeti | yasmātsarvamāpnoti sarvamādatte sarvamatti","ca tasmāducyate ātmeti | atha kasmāducyate maheśvara iti | yasmānmahata","īśaḥ śabdadhvanyā cātmaśaktyā ca mahata īśate tasmāducyate","maheśvara iti | atha kasmāducyate dattātreya iti | yasmātsuduścaraṃ","tapastapyamānāyātraye putrakāmāyātitarāṃ tuṣṭena bhagavatā","jyotirmayenātmaiva datto yasmāccānasūyāyāmatrestanayo'bhavattasmāducyate dattātreya iti | atha yo'sya niruktāni veda sa sarvaṃ veda |","atha yo ha vai vidyayainaṃ paramupāste so'hamiti sa brahmavidbhavati ||","atraite ślokā bhavanti ||","dattātreyaṃ śivaṃ śāntamindranīlanibhaṃ prabhum |","ātmamāyārataṃ devamavadhūtaṃ digambaram"],"words":[],"lit":"Then Śāṇḍilya asked Atharvan: \"O Lord, why is the Self called sat-mātra (pure being), of the one essence of consciousness-bliss, the supreme Brahman?\"<br><br>Atharvan said: \"Because it grows (bṛhati) and causes [all] to grow (bṛṃhayati), it is called param-Brahman.<br><br>Why called Ātman? Because it pervades (āpnoti) all, takes (ādatte) all, eats (atti) all — therefore called Ātman.<br><br>Why called Maheśvara? Because by the sound-power (śabda-dhvani) and his Self-power, he lords over (īśate) the great — therefore Maheśvara.<br><br>Why called Dattātreya? Because to Atri who was performing very difficult tapas for the sake of a son — exceedingly pleased — the venerable Light-formed [Lord] gave his Self (ātmaiva datto); and because he was born to Anasūyā as son of Atri — therefore Dattātreya.<br><br>Whoever knows these etymological derivations of his — that one knows all. Whoever worships him as 'I am That' — that one becomes the knower of Brahman.<br><br>[Then these verses arise:]","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§2 · 1","title":"","sa":["भस्मोद्धूलितसर्वाङ्गं जटाजूटधरं विभुम् ।","चतुर्बाहुमुदाराङ्गं प्रफ़ुल्लकमलेक्षणम्"],"iast":["bhasmoddhūlitasarvāṅgaṃ jaṭājūṭadharaṃ vibhum |","caturbāhumudārāṅgaṃ prafullakamalekṣaṇam"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§2 · 2","title":"","sa":["ज्ञानयोगनिधिं विश्वगुरुं योगिजनप्रियम् ।","भक्तानुकंपिनं सर्वसाक्षिणं सिद्धसेवितम्"],"iast":["jñānayoganidhiṃ viśvaguruṃ yogijanapriyam |","bhaktānukaṃpinaṃ sarvasākṣiṇaṃ siddhasevitam"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§2 · 3","title":"","sa":["एवं यः सततं ध्यायेद्देवदेवं सनातनम् ।","स मुक्तः सर्वपापेभ्यो निःश्रेयसमवाप्नुयात्"],"iast":["evaṃ yaḥ satataṃ dhyāyeddevadevaṃ sanātanam |","sa muktaḥ sarvapāpebhyo niḥśreyasamavāpnuyāt"],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"§2 · 4","title":"","sa":["इत्यों सत्यमित्युपनिषत् ॥","इति तृतीयोऽध्यायः","ॐ भद्रं कर्णेभिः श्रुणुयाम देवा भद्रं पश्येमाक्षभिर्यजत्राः ।","स्थिरैरङ्गैस्तुष्टुवा{\\म्+}सस्तनूभिर्व्यशेम देवहितं यदायुः ।","स्वस्ति न इन्द्रो वृद्धश्रवाः । स्वस्ति नः पूषा विश्ववेदाः ।","स्वस्ति नस्तार्क्ष्यो अरिष्टनेमिः स्वस्ति नो बृहस्पतिर्दधातु ॥","ॐ शान्तिः शान्तिः शान्तिः ॥","इति तृतीयोऽध्यायः ॥ ३ ॥"],"iast":["ityoṃ satyamityupaniṣat |","iti tṛtīyo'dhyāyaḥ","oṃ bhadraṃ karṇebhiḥ śruṇuyāma devā bhadraṃ paśyemākṣabhiryajatrāḥ |","sthirairaṅgaistuṣṭuvā{\\m+}sastanūbhirvyaśema devahitaṃ yadāyuḥ |","svasti na indro vṛddhaśravāḥ | svasti naḥ pūṣā viśvavedāḥ |","svasti nastārkṣyo ariṣṭanemiḥ svasti no bṛhaspatirdadhātu ||","oṃ śāntiḥ śāntiḥ śāntiḥ ||","iti tṛtīyo 'dhyāyaḥ || 3 ||  —  \"Thus the Third Chapter.\""],"words":[],"lit":"Closing line of Adhyāya 3:","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["\"Thus OM is truth, says the Upaniṣad.\""]}]},{"t":"","u":[{"ref":"Closing Śānti Mantra","title":"","sa":["ॐ भद्रं कर्णेभिः शृणुयाम देवा भद्रं पश्येमाक्षभिर्यजत्राः ।","स्थिरैरङ्गैस्तुष्टुवांसस्तनूभिर्व्यशेम देवहितं यदायुः ।","स्वस्ति न इन्द्रो वृद्धश्रवाः । स्वस्ति नः पूषा विश्ववेदाः ।","स्वस्ति नस्तार्क्ष्यो अरिष्टनेमिः । स्वस्ति नो बृहस्पतिर्दधातु ॥","ॐ शान्तिः शान्तिः शान्तिः ॥","इति शाण्डिल्योपनिषत्समाप्ता ॥"],"iast":["oṃ bhadraṃ karṇebhiḥ śṛṇuyāma devā bhadraṃ paśyemākṣabhir yajatrāḥ |","sthirair aṅgais tuṣṭuvāṃsas tanūbhir vyaśema devahitaṃ yad āyuḥ |","svasti na indro vṛddhaśravāḥ | svasti naḥ pūṣā viśvavedāḥ |","svasti nas tārkṣyo ariṣṭanemiḥ | svasti no bṛhaspatir dadhātu ||","oṃ śāntiḥ śāntiḥ śāntiḥ ||","iti śāṇḍilyopaniṣat samāptā ||  —  \"Thus ends the Śāṇḍilya Upaniṣad.\""],"words":[],"lit":"\"OM. May we hear what is auspicious through our ears, O Devas; may we see what is auspicious through our eyes, O worshipful ones. May we — sound of limb, praising bodily — attain the life ordained by the gods. May Indra of great fame bless us; may all-knowing Pūṣan bless us; may Tārkṣya of unhindered wheel bless us; may Bṛhaspati grant us welfare. OM. Peace. Peace. Peace.\"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[]},{"ref":"12. Glossary","title":"","sa":[],"words":[["Aṣṭāṅga-yoga","अष्टाङ्गयोग","Eight-limbed yoga"],["Yama","यम","Ethical restraint (10 in this text)"],["Niyama","नियम","Personal observance (10 in this text)"],["Āsana","आसन","Yogic posture (8 enumerated)"],["Prāṇāyāma","प्राणायाम","Breath-discipline"],["Pratyāhāra","प्रत्याहार","Sense-withdrawal (5-fold here)"],["Dhāraṇā","धारणा","Concentration (3-fold here)"],["Dhyāna","ध्यान","Meditation (saguṇa & nirguṇa)"],["Samādhi","समाधि","Union of jīva and paramātma"],["Mitāhāra","मिताहार","Moderate food — leave 1/4 stomach empty"],["Nāḍī","नाडी","Subtle channel (14 principal)"],["Iḍā","इडा","Left nāḍī, lunar channel"],["Piṅgalā","पिङ्गला","Right nāḍī, solar channel"],["Suṣumnā","सुषुम्ना","Central nāḍī, path of liberation"],["Kuṇḍalinī","कुण्डलिनी","Coiled cosmic power at base of spine"],["Prāṇa","प्राण","Vital air (5 + 5 = 10 total)"],["Apāna","अपान","Eliminative vital air"],["Samāna","समान","Digestive/nourishing vital air"],["Vyāna","व्यान","Distributive vital air"],["Udāna","उदान","Upward-rising vital air"],["Mātrā","मात्रा","Time-measure (~1 sec)"],["Pūraka","पूरक","Inhalation"],["Kumbhaka","कुम्भक","Retention"],["Recaka","रेचक","Exhalation"],["Jālandhara-bandha","जालन्धरबन्ध","Throat lock"],["Uḍḍiyāna-bandha","उड्डियानबन्ध","Abdominal lock"],["Mūla-bandha","मूलबन्ध","Root lock"],["Khecarī Mudrā","खेचरीमुद्रा","Sky-walking seal (tongue back, gaze inward)"],["Vaiṣṇavī Mudrā","वैष्णवीमुद्रा","Inner aim, outer gaze, no blinking"],["Manonmanī","मनोन्मनी","Supra-mental state"],["Marma-sthāna","मर्मस्थान","Vital point (18 enumerated)"],["Saṃyama","संयम","Combined dhāraṇā-dhyāna-samādhi at a point"],["Tripuṭī","त्रिपुटी","Triad of knower-known-knowing"],["Niṣkala","निष्कल","Without parts (transcendent Brahman)"],["Sakala","सकल","With parts (manifest divine form)"],["Sakala-Niṣkala","सकलनिष्कल","With and without parts (cosmic-Self)"],["Dattātreya","दत्तात्रेय","Son of Atri, given by the Lord — accessible divine form"]],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":[],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"13. Editions and Sources","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["Sanskrit text used in this document:","Source: Sanskrit Documents Project (sanskritdocuments.org)","File: shandilya.itx — encoded and proofread by Sunder Hattangadi (last updated Feb 2025)","Description: 58/108 in the Muktikā Upaniṣads; Atharva Veda; Yoga Upaniṣad","Standard published editions and translations:","K. Narayanasvami Aiyar, Thirty Minor Upaniṣads (1914) — first complete English translation","T.R. Srinivasa Ayyangar, The Yoga Upaniṣads (Adyar Library, 1938, rev. 1952) — Sanskrit + English of all 20 Yoga Upaniṣads","A.G. Krishna Warrier, The Yoga Upaniṣads (Adyar Library 1952) — scholarly English standard","Swāmī Sivānanda Saraswatī — partial commentary and translation, Divine Life Society","Patrick Olivelle — has not produced a critical edition of the Yoga Upaniṣads (no recent Western critical edition exists)","Online resources:","sanskritdocuments.org — Sanskrit Devanāgarī and IAST text, free download","archive.org — multiple scanned editions of Aiyar (1914) and Ayyangar (1938)"],"kind":"note"},{"ref":"14. Closing","title":"","sa":[],"words":[],"lit":"","para":"","coms":[],"notes":["The Śāṇḍilya Upaniṣad is the most comprehensive single Yoga Upaniṣad outside of Patañjali. Where the Yoga Tattva is compact and the Vijñāna Bhairava is technique-focused, the Śāṇḍilya is encyclopedic — covering ethics, physical practice, subtle anatomy, breath-discipline, sense-mastery, concentration, meditation, samādhi, brahma-vidyā, and the three forms of Brahman.","Three principles to carry forward:","Ten yamas + ten niyamas — the moral foundation is wider than Patañjali's five each. Master mitāhāra and ahiṃsā first, but cultivate all twenty over time.","The subtle body is real and structured. Without working knowledge of the 14 nāḍīs and 10 vāyus, advanced prāṇāyāma is unsafe and ineffective.","Yoga and Knowledge are two means, not two competitions (§7 v.26). Both work; choose what your temperament calls for, and trust both.","\"jñānaṃ jñeyaṃ samaṃ naṣṭaṃ nānyaḥ panthā dvitīyakaḥ\" — \"When knowledge, knowable, and knower are equally destroyed — there is no other, no second path.\" (Śāṇḍilya 1.7.24)","🪔"],"kind":"note"}]}]};
